1
00:00:42,626 --> 00:00:44,127
[staff] Do you still remember him?

2
00:00:44,211 --> 00:00:45,379
Of course.

3
00:00:45,462 --> 00:00:47,130
Who could ever forget him?

4
00:00:47,214 --> 00:00:50,592
Son of a bitch! Best coach ever!

5
00:00:50,676 --> 00:00:52,594
Oh, are we not allowed to curse?

6
00:00:52,678 --> 00:00:54,054
Shit.

7
00:00:54,137 --> 00:00:56,515
Nicole Cordoves, Philippine...!

8
00:00:56,598 --> 00:00:58,034
[clears throat]
Sorry, let me try again.

9
00:00:58,058 --> 00:01:00,519
Philippines!

10
00:01:00,602 --> 00:01:02,038
[Nicole] <i>He taught me to say it like that.</i>

11
00:01:02,062 --> 00:01:05,566
[MJ] I dieted intensely just to maintain
my figure before the pageant.

12
00:01:05,649 --> 00:01:07,818
As in, water therapy.

13
00:01:08,819 --> 00:01:11,113
May I have another glass of water?

14
00:01:11,196 --> 00:01:13,490
What was he like as a pageant coach?

15
00:01:13,574 --> 00:01:15,909
["Reyna" by Michelle Dee playing]

16
00:01:15,993 --> 00:01:17,411
MOTHER BEAUTY

17
00:01:19,454 --> 00:01:20,789
[Nicole] <i>He's…</i>

18
00:01:20,872 --> 00:01:21,957
<i>Strict.</i>

19
00:01:22,040 --> 00:01:23,208
That's how you do it!

20
00:01:23,292 --> 00:01:24,126
You get it?

21
00:01:24,209 --> 00:01:26,128
- Yes, Mother!
- Yes, Mother!

22
00:01:26,211 --> 00:01:29,423
No absences at rehearsal
since he never misses it either.

23
00:01:29,506 --> 00:01:30,549
Controlling.

24
00:01:30,632 --> 00:01:32,009
[Twinkle] <i>Let's go!</i>

25
00:01:32,092 --> 00:01:33,427
Project!

26
00:01:34,052 --> 00:01:35,137
Shoulders back.

27
00:01:35,220 --> 00:01:36,513
Overly competitive.

28
00:01:36,596 --> 00:01:37,764
[Twinkle] <i>Come on!</i> [claps]

29
00:01:37,848 --> 00:01:39,975
Make them feel your presence!

30
00:01:40,058 --> 00:01:42,227
He made me balance all sorts of things.

31
00:01:42,936 --> 00:01:44,855
Books, pillows…

32
00:01:44,938 --> 00:01:45,772
[slurping]

33
00:01:45,856 --> 00:01:47,107
Intimidating.

34
00:01:47,190 --> 00:01:48,483
[Twinkle] Look fierce!

35
00:01:48,567 --> 00:01:50,402
I said "fierce," not constipated!

36
00:01:51,028 --> 00:01:52,195
[sobbing]

37
00:01:52,863 --> 00:01:54,781
- [staff] Please eat first.
- No!

38
00:01:54,865 --> 00:01:56,742
If he hadn't whipped me into shape,

39
00:01:56,825 --> 00:01:58,368
I wouldn't have this crown today.

40
00:01:58,452 --> 00:01:59,870
[Chelsea] <i>That's Mother.</i>

41
00:01:59,953 --> 00:02:02,247
He pushes you to reach your best.

42
00:02:02,331 --> 00:02:04,916
Actually, even better than the best.

43
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:05,834
[Twinkle]<i> No!</i>

44
00:02:05,917 --> 00:02:07,961
They'll strut until their feet bleed,

45
00:02:08,045 --> 00:02:10,005
all for the crown!

46
00:02:10,088 --> 00:02:11,381
- Yes, Mother!
- Yes, Mother!

47
00:02:11,965 --> 00:02:12,841
Strut!

48
00:02:12,924 --> 00:02:14,092
[Carlene] <i>Because of Mother,</i>

49
00:02:14,176 --> 00:02:17,929
I am the first Filipina
to win two national titles.

50
00:02:18,013 --> 00:02:19,931
Look at my two crowns.

51
00:02:20,015 --> 00:02:21,350
[MJ] <i>I may have failed today,</i>

52
00:02:21,433 --> 00:02:23,226
but Mother always told me,

53
00:02:23,310 --> 00:02:26,021
it's not about how many times I fall.

54
00:02:26,688 --> 00:02:28,440
[Nicole] <i>He is not just a coach.</i>

55
00:02:28,982 --> 00:02:30,150
He is a mother.

56
00:02:30,233 --> 00:02:31,443
He mothered us.

57
00:02:31,526 --> 00:02:32,778
You are a mother,

58
00:02:32,861 --> 00:02:33,987
Mother!

59
00:02:35,280 --> 00:02:36,865
[Twinkle] <i>Mother Twinkle.</i>

60
00:02:36,948 --> 00:02:38,700
<i>That's what they call me.</i>

61
00:02:38,784 --> 00:02:39,984
- Twinkle!
- [Twinkle] Huge arms.

62
00:02:40,035 --> 00:02:42,871
Dear! They rushed your mother
to the hospital!

63
00:02:42,954 --> 00:02:43,954
Huh?

64
00:02:47,459 --> 00:02:51,421
[Twinkle] <i>Just when I thought</i>
<i>I knew everything about being a mother,</i>

65
00:02:51,505 --> 00:02:52,756
<i>you came.</i>

66
00:02:53,507 --> 00:02:54,716
Twinkle,

67
00:02:55,217 --> 00:02:57,636
what will happen to your mom's ward?

68
00:02:58,345 --> 00:02:59,846
You're taking over.

69
00:03:02,641 --> 00:03:06,353
[Mama M] Here, hold the baby
while I take care of the guests.

70
00:03:09,356 --> 00:03:11,400
[Twinkle] <i>Can I be a mother?</i>

71
00:03:11,483 --> 00:03:15,987
[baby fussing]

72
00:03:28,458 --> 00:03:29,876
[baby crying]

73
00:03:29,960 --> 00:03:30,794
Hi, dear.

74
00:03:30,877 --> 00:03:32,129
Let's start.

75
00:03:32,212 --> 00:03:33,630
Start what, Mother?

76
00:03:33,713 --> 00:03:36,383
I've been waiting for you for three hours.

77
00:03:36,466 --> 00:03:38,552
Everyone from our meeting
has already left.

78
00:03:39,136 --> 00:03:42,180
I'm sorry. I had no one
to leave the baby with, poor thing.

79
00:03:42,264 --> 00:03:46,601
I convinced the board of Miss Uniworld
to make Mother Beauty a partner

80
00:03:46,685 --> 00:03:48,395
because I believe in you!

81
00:03:48,478 --> 00:03:51,732
Even if everyone else is saying
that you've lost your touch.

82
00:03:51,815 --> 00:03:53,525
Oh no! What's wrong, baby?

83
00:03:53,608 --> 00:03:54,943
Oh no, he threw up.

84
00:03:55,026 --> 00:03:57,227
- Wait a minute. Oh no, not now.
- [baby continues crying]

85
00:03:57,821 --> 00:03:59,239
At least get me a tissue!

86
00:04:00,407 --> 00:04:01,533
It's okay, baby.

87
00:04:02,117 --> 00:04:04,786
[Twinkle]<i> Can I give you</i>
<i>everything you need?</i>

88
00:04:05,746 --> 00:04:07,330
Were you the one who called earlier?

89
00:04:07,414 --> 00:04:09,207
Yes, ma'am. Here are all my things.

90
00:04:09,291 --> 00:04:10,709
Let me see.

91
00:04:10,792 --> 00:04:12,586
Baby, I'm just selling some stuff, okay?

92
00:04:12,669 --> 00:04:14,045
Take this.

93
00:04:14,129 --> 00:04:15,338
Here you go.

94
00:04:15,422 --> 00:04:17,883
Madam, I don't think
this fairly covers everything.

95
00:04:17,966 --> 00:04:19,801
I'm sure we can get the price higher.

96
00:04:19,885 --> 00:04:21,094
- My baby is sick.
- Oh dear.

97
00:04:21,178 --> 00:04:22,554
Sure, there's a lot,

98
00:04:22,637 --> 00:04:24,139
but it's old and worn out.

99
00:04:24,222 --> 00:04:25,575
It's not worth much, to be honest.

100
00:04:25,599 --> 00:04:27,309
There are crowns and trophies there.

101
00:04:27,392 --> 00:04:30,061
My pageant daughters won them overseas!

102
00:04:30,145 --> 00:04:32,189
Oh, that's true, sis!

103
00:04:32,272 --> 00:04:34,399
And those were big-deal pageants!
Prestigious!

104
00:04:34,483 --> 00:04:36,318
I don't care. Take care of your sick baby.

105
00:04:36,401 --> 00:04:37,402
Go home.

106
00:04:37,486 --> 00:04:39,630
- I'll figure something out. Come on.
- But this is not enough.

107
00:04:39,654 --> 00:04:41,990
Let it go. I already called backup.

108
00:04:42,073 --> 00:04:43,533
[baby crying loudly]

109
00:04:43,617 --> 00:04:44,493
Final answer?

110
00:04:44,576 --> 00:04:46,036
- It's okay.
- Are you sure about this?

111
00:04:46,119 --> 00:04:50,290
You're taking the baby to the orphanage?
I thought you'd grown attached.

112
00:04:51,166 --> 00:04:53,627
I'm completely exhausted, Mama M.

113
00:04:53,710 --> 00:04:56,254
I honestly don't know what to do anymore.

114
00:04:56,880 --> 00:04:58,799
I'm really panicking.

115
00:04:58,882 --> 00:05:00,943
[Mama M] Your mother died
at the worst possible time!

116
00:05:00,967 --> 00:05:02,844
Wait, baby. I need to get dressed.

117
00:05:02,928 --> 00:05:04,596
Be quiet for a second.

118
00:05:04,679 --> 00:05:08,350
- [snaps]
- [baby crying]

119
00:05:10,227 --> 00:05:11,061
Angelo!

120
00:05:11,144 --> 00:05:12,938
- What happened?
- He swallowed a bead!

121
00:05:13,021 --> 00:05:14,624
- Let's take him to the hospital!
- Spit it out!

122
00:05:14,648 --> 00:05:15,941
[Twinkle] Oh my God!

123
00:05:16,024 --> 00:05:17,651
Spit out the bead!

124
00:05:17,734 --> 00:05:18,735
[tense music playing]

125
00:05:18,819 --> 00:05:19,986
Help!

126
00:05:20,946 --> 00:05:21,988
Help!

127
00:05:22,072 --> 00:05:23,824
Help!

128
00:05:26,701 --> 00:05:28,411
Help!

129
00:05:28,495 --> 00:05:30,580
- Please help us! Help!
- [man] What is it?

130
00:05:30,664 --> 00:05:33,333
- Tricycle! Please help us!
- [engine revving]

131
00:05:33,416 --> 00:05:35,126
Mister! Take us to the hospital!

132
00:05:35,210 --> 00:05:37,587
- [car honking]
- Taxi! Please, stop!

133
00:05:37,671 --> 00:05:39,756
- Help! Mister!
- [driver] Hey!

134
00:05:39,839 --> 00:05:42,717
[tense music continues]

135
00:05:42,801 --> 00:05:44,177
Excuse me!

136
00:05:55,897 --> 00:05:59,776
[tense music continues]

137
00:06:03,446 --> 00:06:04,823
[onlookers] Oh my!

138
00:06:04,906 --> 00:06:05,782
The baby!

139
00:06:05,865 --> 00:06:06,783
Help!

140
00:06:06,866 --> 00:06:08,827
- What happened?
- Help! The baby!

141
00:06:08,910 --> 00:06:10,763
- Help the baby! Save him!
- [woman] Oh my, the baby!

142
00:06:10,787 --> 00:06:12,914
- [nurse] Yes, ma'am.
- The baby.

143
00:06:12,998 --> 00:06:14,541
- [whimpers]
- [woman] Oh my!

144
00:06:14,624 --> 00:06:16,543
- Are you all right, ma'am?
- The baby.

145
00:06:16,626 --> 00:06:18,128
[concerned gasps]

146
00:06:18,211 --> 00:06:20,189
[Mama M] <i>You're gonna make</i>
<i>my bangs fall off from worry!</i>

147
00:06:20,213 --> 00:06:21,506
What if you got hurt?

148
00:06:21,590 --> 00:06:23,008
You just took off like that!

149
00:06:23,091 --> 00:06:24,759
You almost flew with the baby!

150
00:06:24,843 --> 00:06:26,553
I panicked, Mama M.

151
00:06:26,636 --> 00:06:29,014
I blacked out.

152
00:06:29,097 --> 00:06:30,097
Oh, God.

153
00:06:30,640 --> 00:06:33,602
I would never forgive myself
if anything bad happened to Angelo.

154
00:06:33,685 --> 00:06:34,603
So, what now?

155
00:06:34,686 --> 00:06:36,521
Your beauty queen legs
are all scratched up.

156
00:06:38,440 --> 00:06:40,025
[doctor] The baby is safe now.

157
00:06:40,108 --> 00:06:41,860
- We retrieved the bead.
- Oh, thank God.

158
00:06:41,943 --> 00:06:43,820
By the way, who are the baby's parents?

159
00:06:43,903 --> 00:06:44,946
I am!

160
00:06:46,031 --> 00:06:47,198
I'm his mother.

161
00:06:47,282 --> 00:06:50,285
[doctor] I'll also get
your discharge papers ready.

162
00:06:50,368 --> 00:06:51,870
I'll leave you here for now.

163
00:06:51,953 --> 00:06:53,371
[Mama M] Thank you, Doctor.

164
00:06:57,626 --> 00:06:59,419
[Twinkle] <i>People always ask,</i>

165
00:06:59,502 --> 00:07:01,838
<i>how are children made?</i>

166
00:07:04,633 --> 00:07:06,092
<i>But me?</i>

167
00:07:07,886 --> 00:07:09,638
<i>I want to know…</i>

168
00:07:11,765 --> 00:07:13,141
Angelo?

169
00:07:14,225 --> 00:07:16,478
<i>How does one become a mother?</i>

170
00:07:17,103 --> 00:07:21,942
[bright music playing]

171
00:07:33,286 --> 00:07:36,039
You should've gotten ready
instead of painting.

172
00:07:36,122 --> 00:07:37,540
- [woman] Hi, Angelo!
- Hello!

173
00:07:37,624 --> 00:07:39,084
- Good morning, Mother.
- Good morning.

174
00:07:39,167 --> 00:07:40,961
You'll be late again.

175
00:07:41,044 --> 00:07:42,921
Shall we hang these on the wall?

176
00:07:43,004 --> 00:07:43,880
Sure!

177
00:07:43,964 --> 00:07:45,131
Good morning!

178
00:07:45,215 --> 00:07:47,401
- [Angelo] Good morning!
- I brought breakfast for my godchild!

179
00:07:47,425 --> 00:07:49,010
[Angelo] Looks yummy!

180
00:07:49,094 --> 00:07:50,863
That looks like our leftovers
from last night, Ma.

181
00:07:50,887 --> 00:07:51,721
Morning, Mother!

182
00:07:51,805 --> 00:07:54,391
- You ate dinner with us, didn't you?
- You cooked for so many.

183
00:07:54,474 --> 00:07:57,495
It would have been a waste to leave them.
We even have enough left for breakfast.

184
00:07:57,519 --> 00:07:59,062
Let me make coffee first.

185
00:07:59,145 --> 00:08:01,314
[Twinkle] Shameless as ever.

186
00:08:01,398 --> 00:08:02,565
Good morning, sis.

187
00:08:02,649 --> 00:08:05,652
Mayet, did you heat water
for Angelo's bath?

188
00:08:05,735 --> 00:08:07,862
- I forgot, sis! Sorry!
- Geez!

189
00:08:07,946 --> 00:08:10,323
Mother, don't blow your top!

190
00:08:11,574 --> 00:08:13,868
You'd better put away
all your mess afterward.

191
00:08:13,952 --> 00:08:15,161
What are you making?

192
00:08:15,245 --> 00:08:18,373
We're making placards
for the rally, Mother.

193
00:08:18,456 --> 00:08:19,332
Rally?

194
00:08:19,416 --> 00:08:21,584
Girl, I thought this was
for the Bini concert?

195
00:08:21,668 --> 00:08:22,502
Bini?

196
00:08:22,585 --> 00:08:24,504
But your face looks like wasabi?

197
00:08:24,587 --> 00:08:26,673
- Mother, we have a play later.
- [Bea] Marco!

198
00:08:26,756 --> 00:08:29,718
Hey! If you make me late,
you're going to be our cadaver in class!

199
00:08:29,801 --> 00:08:31,803
What? What's Bea saying?

200
00:08:31,886 --> 00:08:33,888
Marco's taking forever in the shower.

201
00:08:33,972 --> 00:08:37,183
Ma! My painting fell!

202
00:08:40,228 --> 00:08:41,938
Wow!

203
00:08:42,022 --> 00:08:45,859
You're getting better at this.

204
00:08:45,942 --> 00:08:47,610
Let's hang it over there!

205
00:08:47,694 --> 00:08:49,320
Morning, Mother.

206
00:08:51,197 --> 00:08:52,532
How about this spot?

207
00:08:52,615 --> 00:08:53,533
[Angelo] Yes, Ma.

208
00:08:53,616 --> 00:08:54,993
There. All displayed.

209
00:08:55,076 --> 00:08:56,161
[Angelo] Yay!

210
00:08:56,244 --> 00:08:58,872
[Mama M gasps] Twinkle!
Come here! Hurry up!

211
00:08:58,955 --> 00:09:00,957
Mama, what's wrong?
Are you having a heart attack?

212
00:09:01,041 --> 00:09:02,393
Hold your breath and see for yourself.

213
00:09:02,417 --> 00:09:04,520
[reporter on TV] <i>Beauty queen</i>
<i>Mara De Jesus is now engaged</i>

214
00:09:04,544 --> 00:09:08,298
<i>to the heir of Villaverde Corporation,</i>

215
00:09:08,381 --> 00:09:10,216
<i>Anton Villaverde.</i>

216
00:09:10,300 --> 00:09:12,552
<i>Mara happily showed off</i>

217
00:09:12,635 --> 00:09:16,389
<i>her 24,000-carat octagon-cut
diamond engagement ring.</i>

218
00:09:16,473 --> 00:09:19,225
<i>- Fully paid!</i>
- It's too early for this nonsense.

219
00:09:19,309 --> 00:09:20,518
[turns off TV]

220
00:09:20,602 --> 00:09:22,062
She looks like an angel, Ma!

221
00:09:22,145 --> 00:09:23,438
She's so beautiful!

222
00:09:24,355 --> 00:09:25,857
She's not an angel, sweetie. Come on.

223
00:09:25,940 --> 00:09:27,067
Time for your bath, okay?

224
00:09:27,150 --> 00:09:28,150
[Angelo] Yes, Ma.

225
00:09:29,569 --> 00:09:30,713
Ma'am, what makeup do you want?

226
00:09:30,737 --> 00:09:31,613
Lipstick?

227
00:09:31,696 --> 00:09:32,696
Eyebrows?

228
00:09:32,739 --> 00:09:34,491
Maybe some blush.

229
00:09:34,574 --> 00:09:35,734
You're looking a little pale.

230
00:09:37,368 --> 00:09:38,661
[Mama M] Twinkle! Dear!

231
00:09:38,745 --> 00:09:40,622
Mama M!

232
00:09:40,705 --> 00:09:42,290
How are you? Where'd you come from?

233
00:09:42,832 --> 00:09:43,833
Who's this with you?

234
00:09:44,459 --> 00:09:45,960
Good day, mate!

235
00:09:46,044 --> 00:09:47,170
Oh my God!

236
00:09:48,004 --> 00:09:49,004
Dorothy?

237
00:09:49,464 --> 00:09:50,464
I know!

238
00:09:50,507 --> 00:09:51,800
Bonkers, right?

239
00:09:51,883 --> 00:09:53,593
[Twinkle] Is that really you?

240
00:09:53,676 --> 00:09:55,470
But you look so pretty! Do a spin!

241
00:09:56,387 --> 00:09:57,555
Oh my! She's really grown!

242
00:09:57,639 --> 00:09:59,057
[Twinkle] Yes!

243
00:09:59,140 --> 00:10:01,726
Peppa Pig is green now.
I thought she was pink?

244
00:10:01,810 --> 00:10:03,520
- You're such a joker.
- How are you?

245
00:10:03,603 --> 00:10:07,065
Still the most gorgeous
and delectable Filipina in Hong Kong!

246
00:10:07,148 --> 00:10:08,584
- You're now based in Hong Kong?
- Yes!

247
00:10:08,608 --> 00:10:10,068
- She came from Hong Kong?
- Yes.

248
00:10:10,151 --> 00:10:11,545
I was actually planning to visit you.

249
00:10:11,569 --> 00:10:15,532
But Mama M said that
this is where to find you.

250
00:10:15,615 --> 00:10:17,575
This is my gig for now.

251
00:10:17,659 --> 00:10:18,576
You know how it is.

252
00:10:18,660 --> 00:10:21,037
Pageant money isn't steady.

253
00:10:21,121 --> 00:10:22,413
Most days, nada.

254
00:10:22,497 --> 00:10:23,665
So this is my hustle for now.

255
00:10:23,748 --> 00:10:26,084
Exactly, sis!

256
00:10:26,167 --> 00:10:27,669
I came here on purpose

257
00:10:27,752 --> 00:10:30,922
to let you know there are
lots of openings again

258
00:10:31,005 --> 00:10:32,465
next year at Disneyland!

259
00:10:32,549 --> 00:10:33,633
- Disneyland?
- Yes!

260
00:10:33,716 --> 00:10:35,093
- For real?
- Yes!

261
00:10:35,176 --> 00:10:36,928
I told you he'd love this news!

262
00:10:37,011 --> 00:10:40,223
It's been his dream to go abroad!

263
00:10:40,306 --> 00:10:41,683
Go for it, dear!

264
00:10:41,766 --> 00:10:43,685
Dorothy will oversee everything.

265
00:10:43,768 --> 00:10:45,353
I won't just oversee,

266
00:10:45,436 --> 00:10:47,480
I'll run the whole process for my bestie!

267
00:10:47,564 --> 00:10:49,691
Because our agency

268
00:10:49,774 --> 00:10:51,943
is looking for hotel receptionists.

269
00:10:52,026 --> 00:10:54,404
- Really?
- [Dorothy] Mm-hm.

270
00:10:55,864 --> 00:10:58,783
But, Mama M, you know I have a kid, right?

271
00:10:58,867 --> 00:11:01,452
I can't just leave Angelo like that.

272
00:11:01,536 --> 00:11:03,037
What a shame.

273
00:11:03,121 --> 00:11:05,623
[Dorothy] No problem! Take him with you!

274
00:11:06,499 --> 00:11:08,293
[Dorothy] <i>If you want to go to Disneyland,</i>

275
00:11:08,376 --> 00:11:10,753
<i>you need a passport.</i>

276
00:11:10,837 --> 00:11:12,797
[Dorothy] Yes, sis, a passport!

277
00:11:12,881 --> 00:11:14,507
I hope your kid has one.

278
00:11:14,591 --> 00:11:16,593
Birth certificate, Form 137,

279
00:11:16,676 --> 00:11:17,594
all the papers.

280
00:11:17,677 --> 00:11:18,821
You have those, right? Right?

281
00:11:18,845 --> 00:11:20,013
Well…

282
00:11:20,096 --> 00:11:22,056
My godchild doesn't have any of that yet

283
00:11:22,140 --> 00:11:25,685
because Twinkle
hasn't legally adopted him.

284
00:11:26,561 --> 00:11:27,687
Too bad.

285
00:11:28,313 --> 00:11:30,982
And Angelo's always dreamt
of going to Disneyland.

286
00:11:31,733 --> 00:11:32,817
What a waste.

287
00:11:33,526 --> 00:11:35,111
If only there was a way…

288
00:11:35,194 --> 00:11:36,863
[sighs]

289
00:11:36,946 --> 00:11:38,406
Don't give me this mopey crap!

290
00:11:38,489 --> 00:11:40,074
Go for it, girl!

291
00:11:40,158 --> 00:11:41,284
They're just papers.

292
00:11:41,868 --> 00:11:44,037
[Dorothy] Get that adoption
sorted out already.

293
00:11:44,120 --> 00:11:46,414
Otherwise, it'll be a waste
of a good opportunity.

294
00:11:47,123 --> 00:11:49,334
I'm sorry, sweetie.
I couldn't pick you up earlier.

295
00:11:49,417 --> 00:11:51,669
I had to finish a lot of work.

296
00:11:51,753 --> 00:11:53,046
That's okay.

297
00:11:53,129 --> 00:11:56,132
I finished all my assignments
while waiting for you.

298
00:11:56,215 --> 00:11:59,469
Wow, you're really amazing.

299
00:11:59,552 --> 00:12:01,804
- Of course! I take after you!
- Stay here.

300
00:12:01,888 --> 00:12:02,764
Oh, please!

301
00:12:02,847 --> 00:12:03,973
And you know what?

302
00:12:04,057 --> 00:12:06,851
I was the only one
who got 100 in spelling today.

303
00:12:06,935 --> 00:12:09,812
Wow! I'm so proud of you!

304
00:12:09,896 --> 00:12:11,689
I even told my teacher

305
00:12:11,773 --> 00:12:13,524
that ever since I was a baby,

306
00:12:13,608 --> 00:12:15,151
you've taught me how to write.

307
00:12:15,234 --> 00:12:16,110
Correct.

308
00:12:16,194 --> 00:12:18,404
That's why you stand out.
You're the best!

309
00:12:19,489 --> 00:12:22,075
And because of that,
I feel like giving you a reward.

310
00:12:22,158 --> 00:12:26,704
Didn't you promise me for my birthday
that you'd buy me that bike?

311
00:12:29,749 --> 00:12:31,084
[bell rings]

312
00:12:31,167 --> 00:12:32,377
Yes, I did!

313
00:12:32,919 --> 00:12:36,130
I'm already saving up for that, sweetie.
That would be yours on your birthday.

314
00:12:36,214 --> 00:12:38,049
[Twinkle] Don't worry,

315
00:12:38,132 --> 00:12:40,468
I won't just give you a bike.

316
00:12:40,551 --> 00:12:41,594
On your birthday,

317
00:12:41,678 --> 00:12:43,388
we're going to Disneyland!

318
00:12:43,471 --> 00:12:44,764
[Twinkle] Would you like that?

319
00:12:47,183 --> 00:12:50,395
I love you, Mama! Mwah! Mwah!

320
00:12:50,478 --> 00:12:52,647
Aw, aren't you the sweetest?

321
00:12:52,730 --> 00:12:55,233
One more time, just to be sure.
Tell me again what you said?

322
00:12:55,316 --> 00:12:57,735
I love you, I love you, I love you!

323
00:12:59,654 --> 00:13:01,072
[Angelo] Mwah!

324
00:13:02,615 --> 00:13:04,117
[Mutya] Here, please read this.

325
00:13:05,702 --> 00:13:08,496
You and Angelo

326
00:13:08,579 --> 00:13:09,914
will have counseling sessions

327
00:13:09,998 --> 00:13:12,375
together with his biological mother.

328
00:13:14,002 --> 00:13:16,879
This is such a long process
to adopt my own child.

329
00:13:16,963 --> 00:13:20,675
Can't I just post it on social media
and tag all of them?

330
00:13:20,758 --> 00:13:22,385
[Mutya chuckles] Oh, no.

331
00:13:22,468 --> 00:13:23,553
No?

332
00:13:23,636 --> 00:13:26,139
So we can get started,

333
00:13:27,557 --> 00:13:30,518
do you know Angelo's biological mother?

334
00:13:33,187 --> 00:13:34,397
Go on, tell her.

335
00:13:38,651 --> 00:13:39,819
Yes, it's…

336
00:13:39,902 --> 00:13:41,070
Mara De Jesus.

337
00:13:42,321 --> 00:13:43,865
[Mutya] <i>Mara De Jesus?</i>

338
00:13:43,948 --> 00:13:46,826
<i>The beauty queen slash model,</i>

339
00:13:46,909 --> 00:13:48,327
<i>slash philanthropist,</i>

340
00:13:48,411 --> 00:13:50,580
<i>slash humanitarian aid,</i>

341
00:13:50,663 --> 00:13:51,914
<i>slash influencer,</i>

342
00:13:51,998 --> 00:13:56,586
<i>slash Woman of the Year awardee
of In Times Magazine 2025?</i>

343
00:13:56,669 --> 00:13:59,589
Correct! With a big fat check!

344
00:14:00,590 --> 00:14:01,590
That's her.

345
00:14:02,175 --> 00:14:03,760
Mara.

346
00:14:04,469 --> 00:14:06,304
- [man] Miss Mara!
- [reporter] Miss Mara!

347
00:14:06,387 --> 00:14:09,515
Have you heard that the age restriction

348
00:14:09,599 --> 00:14:11,851
for Miss Uniworld Philippines
has been lifted?

349
00:14:11,934 --> 00:14:14,187
If so, will you join?

350
00:14:14,729 --> 00:14:16,647
- [man] Miss Mara!
- [cameras clicking]

351
00:14:20,568 --> 00:14:22,779
[Twinkle] <i>She was my student</i>
<i>back at Mother Beauty</i>

352
00:14:22,862 --> 00:14:25,073
<i>when I was still coaching beauty queens.</i>

353
00:14:25,156 --> 00:14:29,744
Thank you, everyone! Thank you! Mara has
other commitments to attend, okay?

354
00:14:29,827 --> 00:14:31,162
- Thank you!
- [reporters clamoring]

355
00:14:31,245 --> 00:14:32,663
- Cut it out!
- [clamoring stops]

356
00:14:32,747 --> 00:14:34,248
I won't say it again!

357
00:14:34,332 --> 00:14:35,792
[silence]

358
00:14:37,126 --> 00:14:38,687
- [man 1 and 2] Miss Mara!
- [crowd clamoring]

359
00:14:38,711 --> 00:14:40,380
[Mutya] <i>Scandalous!</i>

360
00:14:40,463 --> 00:14:43,633
So how did her child end up with you?

361
00:14:44,300 --> 00:14:45,635
Here's the thing.

362
00:14:45,718 --> 00:14:49,055
Remember the last time
she joined Miss Uniworld?

363
00:14:49,138 --> 00:14:51,015
Yes! That went viral!

364
00:14:51,099 --> 00:14:52,016
Exactly!

365
00:14:52,100 --> 00:14:54,394
Should a woman have to choose

366
00:14:54,477 --> 00:14:58,022
if your ultimate dream
required a long-term commitment

367
00:14:58,106 --> 00:15:00,942
that takes you away from
your future child,

368
00:15:01,025 --> 00:15:03,569
which would you choose to honor,

369
00:15:03,653 --> 00:15:04,821
your career

370
00:15:04,904 --> 00:15:06,406
or your child?

371
00:15:06,489 --> 00:15:09,826
[breathing heavily]

372
00:15:09,909 --> 00:15:12,537
[Twinkle] <i>She was</i>
<i>already pregnant with Angelo then.</i>

373
00:15:12,620 --> 00:15:15,081
- [man] Medic! Get a medic!
- [Mutya]<i> OMG!</i>

374
00:15:15,164 --> 00:15:17,667
[Mila] <i>You are pregnant?!</i>

375
00:15:17,750 --> 00:15:20,378
How can you be pregnant?

376
00:15:20,461 --> 00:15:21,295
Huh?

377
00:15:21,379 --> 00:15:23,673
[Twinkle] <i>Her mother, Mila, was furious.</i>

378
00:15:23,756 --> 00:15:25,197
- [Twinkle] <i>Then whack!</i>
- [others gasp]

379
00:15:25,758 --> 00:15:27,427
[Twinkle] <i>She slapped Mara.</i>

380
00:15:27,510 --> 00:15:30,179
[Mutya] <i>Mila De Jesus?</i>
<i>The one who was also a beauty queen?</i>

381
00:15:30,263 --> 00:15:33,933
Correct, with a big fat check!

382
00:15:34,016 --> 00:15:35,059
[Twinkle] Then…

383
00:15:35,143 --> 00:15:36,018
[Twinkle] <i>Whack!</i>

384
00:15:36,102 --> 00:15:37,246
[Mutya] <i>Who got slapped next?</i>

385
00:15:37,270 --> 00:15:38,510
[Twinkle]<i> There was a mosquito.</i>

386
00:15:38,563 --> 00:15:40,314
<i>I killed it so no one would get dengue.</i>

387
00:15:40,398 --> 00:15:42,733
<i>But the next one, this one was real.
My heart jumped.</i>

388
00:15:42,817 --> 00:15:44,068
- [Twinkle] <i>Whack!</i>
- [others gasp]

389
00:15:44,152 --> 00:15:45,736
This is your fault!

390
00:15:45,820 --> 00:15:49,282
If you had watched over Mara,
she wouldn't have gotten pregnant!

391
00:15:49,365 --> 00:15:51,200
[Twinkle] <i>She slapped Mr. J.</i>

392
00:15:51,284 --> 00:15:52,618
- [whimpers]
- [Twinkle] <i>Full swing.</i>

393
00:15:52,702 --> 00:15:54,763
Then suddenly, even I got startled.
Out of nowhere, whack!

394
00:15:54,787 --> 00:15:58,249
- [Mila gasps]
- This is your fault!

395
00:15:58,332 --> 00:16:01,752
She's your daughter!
She is your responsibility!

396
00:16:01,836 --> 00:16:04,881
[Twinkle] <i>Mila was about</i>
<i>to retaliate! But then!</i>

397
00:16:04,964 --> 00:16:06,382
- You!
- [groans]

398
00:16:06,466 --> 00:16:07,818
[Twinkle] <i>Her hand landed on my face.</i>

399
00:16:07,842 --> 00:16:10,428
Keep your mother in line!

400
00:16:11,804 --> 00:16:13,222
That shook my brain.

401
00:16:13,306 --> 00:16:14,515
Of course, you fought back.

402
00:16:14,599 --> 00:16:15,683
Of course not.

403
00:16:15,766 --> 00:16:16,601
She's rich, remember?

404
00:16:16,684 --> 00:16:18,686
She could've had me
thrown in jail back then.

405
00:16:18,769 --> 00:16:20,229
But I wouldn't just let it go.
Whack!

406
00:16:20,313 --> 00:16:21,564
[gasps]

407
00:16:21,647 --> 00:16:23,441
Why did you slap me this time?

408
00:16:23,524 --> 00:16:26,319
Because you stole Prince Cedi's costume!

409
00:16:27,570 --> 00:16:30,198
[Mila] When you give birth,
we're giving the baby away.

410
00:16:30,281 --> 00:16:31,681
[sobbing] But, Ma, this is my baby.

411
00:16:31,741 --> 00:16:32,658
[Mila] No!

412
00:16:32,742 --> 00:16:33,659
[sobs]

413
00:16:33,743 --> 00:16:35,661
[Mila] Mara, Mara, Mara!

414
00:16:35,745 --> 00:16:37,413
Mara! Mara!

415
00:16:38,748 --> 00:16:41,250
I've long wanted to have a grandchild,

416
00:16:41,334 --> 00:16:43,294
and I can't count on you.

417
00:16:43,836 --> 00:16:46,088
Let's just care for the baby.

418
00:16:48,674 --> 00:16:51,260
- [Mama M screams]
- Don't do it! She's your mother!

419
00:16:51,344 --> 00:16:52,345
You're right.

420
00:16:52,428 --> 00:16:54,555
Sorry, Ma. I was just taken aback.

421
00:16:56,307 --> 00:16:59,268
Ma, I don't think I can let him go.

422
00:16:59,352 --> 00:17:02,104
He'll be with a good family.

423
00:17:03,523 --> 00:17:05,107
[Mila] Just give him up

424
00:17:06,400 --> 00:17:08,611
and live the life you're meant to have.

425
00:17:09,445 --> 00:17:12,365
- [sobbing]
- [somber music playing]

426
00:17:12,448 --> 00:17:13,574
Give me the baby.

427
00:17:15,576 --> 00:17:17,203
Ma, please. Please.

428
00:17:17,286 --> 00:17:18,286
- Please.
- Mara!

429
00:17:19,830 --> 00:17:22,833
- [soft sob]
- [tragic orchestral music swells]

430
00:17:24,377 --> 00:17:25,586
[Twinkle] <i>One day,</i>

431
00:17:26,671 --> 00:17:29,465
<i>my mother just showed up with a baby.</i>

432
00:17:29,549 --> 00:17:30,925
[sobbing]

433
00:17:31,008 --> 00:17:32,343
[Twinkle] <i>Angelo.</i>

434
00:17:33,427 --> 00:17:36,097
<i>It turns out,
Mila gave Mara's child to her.</i>

435
00:17:38,599 --> 00:17:40,268
After my mother passed,

436
00:17:41,227 --> 00:17:42,436
well,

437
00:17:42,520 --> 00:17:44,897
I became Angelo's mother.

438
00:17:44,981 --> 00:17:45,981
[Mutya] Unbelievable.

439
00:17:46,899 --> 00:17:48,693
Like something out of a soap opera.

440
00:17:50,069 --> 00:17:51,279
[Mutya] So here's the deal.

441
00:17:51,362 --> 00:17:53,823
Do you still have contact with Mara?

442
00:17:57,952 --> 00:18:00,371
For this to happen,

443
00:18:00,454 --> 00:18:03,165
we need her signature.

444
00:18:04,875 --> 00:18:11,340
[pensive music playing]

445
00:18:15,761 --> 00:18:19,140
[sniffles, sobs]

446
00:18:30,526 --> 00:18:32,903
[Ms. J] That long face
doesn't really suit you.

447
00:18:34,947 --> 00:18:37,783
I've known about the Miss Uniworld thing
since last week.

448
00:18:40,494 --> 00:18:43,581
But whenever it comes up,
I still think of him.

449
00:18:46,167 --> 00:18:49,337
I wonder if he's doing okay now.

450
00:18:51,339 --> 00:18:53,841
You need to focus on the future.

451
00:18:53,924 --> 00:18:55,593
On your wedding with Anton.

452
00:18:56,802 --> 00:18:58,971
Not on all those what-ifs.

453
00:19:00,014 --> 00:19:02,183
[Ms. J] And tonight,
you'll be meeting his parents.

454
00:19:02,266 --> 00:19:04,935
So fix your face.
You don't look like a winner.

455
00:19:11,984 --> 00:19:13,319
[Nanette] <i>You know what, Mara.</i>

456
00:19:13,402 --> 00:19:15,154
<i>I really admire you.</i>

457
00:19:16,155 --> 00:19:21,077
Even with so many people
meddling in your personal lives,

458
00:19:21,827 --> 00:19:23,954
you don't seem affected.

459
00:19:24,747 --> 00:19:28,042
Me? I'm fed up.

460
00:19:28,125 --> 00:19:32,213
So many reporters keep calling our house,

461
00:19:32,296 --> 00:19:35,257
wanting interviews with Tony and me
about your wedding.

462
00:19:36,634 --> 00:19:38,469
Sorry, Auntie.

463
00:19:38,552 --> 00:19:41,180
I know you're private people.

464
00:19:41,847 --> 00:19:44,308
Maybe just ignore it.

465
00:19:45,184 --> 00:19:49,063
Just give us a grandchild soon, okay?

466
00:19:49,146 --> 00:19:50,231
[Anton] Dad,

467
00:19:50,314 --> 00:19:52,584
you make it sound like you don't have
a grandchild from Andy.

468
00:19:52,608 --> 00:19:55,152
What are you saying?
He's adopted.

469
00:19:56,320 --> 00:19:59,865
[Nanette] What your dad means is,

470
00:19:59,949 --> 00:20:01,867
family by blood is different, right?

471
00:20:02,743 --> 00:20:04,704
So, when is the wedding?

472
00:20:06,956 --> 00:20:07,957
Next year.

473
00:20:08,666 --> 00:20:10,584
[Nanette] Aren't you moving to the States?

474
00:20:10,668 --> 00:20:12,128
What's the delay?

475
00:20:18,342 --> 00:20:19,593
Mara and I talked,

476
00:20:19,677 --> 00:20:23,431
and she's about to do something big
before we get married.

477
00:20:23,514 --> 00:20:24,765
And…

478
00:20:25,349 --> 00:20:26,726
I want to support her.

479
00:20:27,810 --> 00:20:29,937
What is it? I wasn't informed.

480
00:20:31,313 --> 00:20:35,359
I want to compete in Miss Uniworld again
before we get married.

481
00:20:36,318 --> 00:20:37,903
I want to win the crown this time.

482
00:20:37,987 --> 00:20:39,447
OMG!

483
00:20:39,530 --> 00:20:41,365
The queen is making a comeback!

484
00:20:42,074 --> 00:20:45,035
[Nanette] Well, if that's
really what you want, Mara.

485
00:20:45,119 --> 00:20:46,495
Just remember,

486
00:20:46,579 --> 00:20:49,373
a crown is only for a year.

487
00:20:49,457 --> 00:20:51,625
A family is forever.

488
00:20:58,924 --> 00:21:00,551
[Mutya] Angelo,

489
00:21:01,343 --> 00:21:04,013
do you understand what's happening?

490
00:21:05,431 --> 00:21:08,934
Are you able to follow what we need to do?

491
00:21:10,603 --> 00:21:11,604
Yes, ma'am.

492
00:21:11,687 --> 00:21:14,815
Mama Twinkle is going to adopt me

493
00:21:14,899 --> 00:21:17,526
so we can go to Disneyland.

494
00:21:18,194 --> 00:21:19,320
That's right.

495
00:21:20,154 --> 00:21:24,033
And once Mama Twinkle adopts you,

496
00:21:24,617 --> 00:21:27,286
that means he's your legal mom.

497
00:21:29,205 --> 00:21:32,041
Do you have any other questions?

498
00:21:41,175 --> 00:21:43,594
Who's my other Mama?

499
00:21:44,845 --> 00:21:46,555
[Angelo] Do I have a Papa?

500
00:21:47,681 --> 00:21:49,767
Do I have siblings?

501
00:21:50,684 --> 00:21:51,727
Cousins?

502
00:21:51,811 --> 00:21:53,270
A grandma and grandpa?

503
00:21:53,854 --> 00:21:55,272
They've all passed away.

504
00:21:56,232 --> 00:21:57,399
Sorry?

505
00:21:57,483 --> 00:21:58,359
No, sweetie.

506
00:21:58,442 --> 00:22:00,277
Easy on the questions, there's too many.

507
00:22:00,361 --> 00:22:03,739
She has a heart condition. She could die.

508
00:22:07,868 --> 00:22:09,036
In time,

509
00:22:09,119 --> 00:22:10,746
we'll explain everything to you,

510
00:22:10,830 --> 00:22:12,498
but for now,

511
00:22:12,581 --> 00:22:15,709
let's focus on getting
your adoption papers in order.

512
00:22:16,293 --> 00:22:17,127
The important thing is,

513
00:22:17,211 --> 00:22:19,755
your Mama loves you very much

514
00:22:19,839 --> 00:22:23,175
and will do his absolute best for you.

515
00:22:25,844 --> 00:22:28,931
[gentle music playing]

516
00:22:33,561 --> 00:22:34,562
Twinkle?

517
00:22:34,645 --> 00:22:36,230
In the flesh.

518
00:22:37,022 --> 00:22:38,899
Who let you in?

519
00:22:38,983 --> 00:22:40,943
The power of the elementals.

520
00:22:41,026 --> 00:22:42,152
If you get my drift.

521
00:22:42,653 --> 00:22:44,071
What brings you here?

522
00:22:45,781 --> 00:22:47,032
I'm here

523
00:22:47,116 --> 00:22:48,325
for my son.

524
00:22:48,409 --> 00:22:49,409
Sign this

525
00:22:49,451 --> 00:22:54,164
so Angelo and I can leave
this godforsaken country,

526
00:22:54,248 --> 00:22:55,708
the Philippines!

527
00:22:56,333 --> 00:22:57,376
[paper rustles]

528
00:22:57,459 --> 00:23:00,838
[tense music playing]

529
00:23:00,921 --> 00:23:04,925
- [paper tears]
- [Twinkle laughs]

530
00:23:08,220 --> 00:23:11,682
[laughs loudly]

531
00:23:11,765 --> 00:23:14,476
That is so predictable.

532
00:23:15,603 --> 00:23:16,937
I prepared another one.

533
00:23:17,855 --> 00:23:19,231
Not for long.

534
00:23:20,858 --> 00:23:21,775
[clicks]

535
00:23:21,859 --> 00:23:24,445
- [Twinkle shrieks]
- [Ms. J laughs]

536
00:23:24,528 --> 00:23:28,198
[laughter]

537
00:23:30,409 --> 00:23:31,994
This is the end for you, Mara!

538
00:23:32,077 --> 00:23:34,121
[maniacal laughter]

539
00:23:34,204 --> 00:23:35,623
Angelo is mine!

540
00:23:37,499 --> 00:23:39,300
- My child is mine!
- [Mara and Ms. J screaming]

541
00:23:39,376 --> 00:23:42,546
[laughing continues]

542
00:23:44,131 --> 00:23:45,633
This is wrong.

543
00:23:48,802 --> 00:23:50,304
Twinkelito…

544
00:23:50,888 --> 00:23:52,264
Paoros Reyes?

545
00:23:53,140 --> 00:23:55,100
Diosdado Patumbong?

546
00:23:56,977 --> 00:23:58,562
You've transitioned?

547
00:23:58,646 --> 00:24:00,314
Yes! Just call me Ms. J.

548
00:24:00,397 --> 00:24:01,565
Twinkle?

549
00:24:05,319 --> 00:24:06,319
Are you

550
00:24:06,737 --> 00:24:08,197
applying to be my coach?

551
00:24:09,281 --> 00:24:10,281
Coach?

552
00:24:12,534 --> 00:24:14,453
I'm here because I need
something from you.

553
00:24:15,913 --> 00:24:17,498
I'm adopting Angelo.

554
00:24:17,581 --> 00:24:19,333
What for? You already have the child.

555
00:24:19,416 --> 00:24:21,877
Because of your dry burgundy hair,
we're leaving the country,

556
00:24:21,960 --> 00:24:23,712
so he needs documents.

557
00:24:23,796 --> 00:24:25,464
Which means I need to legally adopt him.

558
00:24:25,547 --> 00:24:27,216
Which means I need your help.

559
00:24:28,926 --> 00:24:30,052
Okay.

560
00:24:30,135 --> 00:24:31,387
I'll help you.

561
00:24:31,470 --> 00:24:33,013
- Are you sure?
- But!

562
00:24:33,764 --> 00:24:37,309
Only if you agree to be my coach
for the upcoming Miss Uniworld.

563
00:24:37,976 --> 00:24:39,937
[Ms. J] Mara, think this through.

564
00:24:40,020 --> 00:24:42,856
What if they find out about the kid?
That would be a scandal!

565
00:24:44,274 --> 00:24:45,943
I want to get the crown.

566
00:24:46,735 --> 00:24:48,946
And you're the only one that can help me.

567
00:24:49,530 --> 00:24:51,949
I need a strict, heartless,

568
00:24:52,032 --> 00:24:54,993
