that will make me win.

569
00:24:55,077 --> 00:24:55,994
Wow.

570
00:24:56,078 --> 00:24:57,746
I sound terrible in your story.

571
00:24:58,330 --> 00:24:59,498
I need the best.

572
00:25:00,165 --> 00:25:01,333
So I need you.

573
00:25:02,126 --> 00:25:04,586
And I'm also the only one
who can help you.

574
00:25:04,670 --> 00:25:07,131
I gave up pageant coaching
a long time ago.

575
00:25:09,216 --> 00:25:10,509
Twinkle, please.

576
00:25:12,094 --> 00:25:13,512
I trust you.

577
00:25:19,685 --> 00:25:21,562
[squeaking]

578
00:25:22,312 --> 00:25:23,605
[Mama M] Hey! Enough!

579
00:25:23,689 --> 00:25:24,833
You've been at that for forever!

580
00:25:24,857 --> 00:25:27,234
Are you trying to scrub
a hole in that pan?

581
00:25:27,317 --> 00:25:29,445
What exactly happened? Did Mara agree?

582
00:25:29,528 --> 00:25:30,571
- [squeaks]
- [grunts]

583
00:25:32,114 --> 00:25:33,741
- She agreed!
- [water running]

584
00:25:35,159 --> 00:25:36,160
But she has conditions.

585
00:25:36,243 --> 00:25:38,495
Oh! What conditions?

586
00:25:40,247 --> 00:25:42,499
She said she'll only help

587
00:25:43,584 --> 00:25:45,294
if I train her for Miss Uniworld.

588
00:25:45,377 --> 00:25:46,670
Unbelievable, right?

589
00:25:46,754 --> 00:25:48,213
- Wow!
- What "wow"?

590
00:25:48,297 --> 00:25:49,465
A reunion!

591
00:25:49,548 --> 00:25:52,092
And if it happens,
it's a comeback for both of you.

592
00:25:52,176 --> 00:25:54,887
Maybe Mara just wants to prove

593
00:25:54,970 --> 00:25:56,847
she deserves the crown.

594
00:25:56,930 --> 00:25:59,183
And you, you'll prove

595
00:25:59,266 --> 00:26:02,895
that you're still the best pageant coach.

596
00:26:02,978 --> 00:26:05,230
No! No! No! That's not happening, Mama!

597
00:26:05,814 --> 00:26:09,610
If I do that, it's like giving her
a chance to get closer to…

598
00:26:10,486 --> 00:26:11,820
To Angelo.

599
00:26:11,904 --> 00:26:13,280
To her son.

600
00:26:13,822 --> 00:26:16,116
What if she takes him away from me?

601
00:26:16,200 --> 00:26:17,367
Shh!

602
00:26:17,451 --> 00:26:20,746
Set boundaries. Keep it professional.

603
00:26:20,829 --> 00:26:22,623
- No personal matters!
- Boundaries?

604
00:26:23,165 --> 00:26:25,167
Just meet at the studio.

605
00:26:25,250 --> 00:26:27,085
Never here at home.

606
00:26:28,295 --> 00:26:30,339
I don't like it. Absolutely not.

607
00:26:30,839 --> 00:26:32,341
My God,

608
00:26:32,424 --> 00:26:34,343
of all people!

609
00:26:34,843 --> 00:26:40,641
Why does Mara De Jesus
have to be Angelo's real mother?

610
00:26:40,724 --> 00:26:45,103
My God! Beautiful, rich, influential.
How do I compete with that?

611
00:26:45,187 --> 00:26:48,732
- I'm terrified she might take him back.
- Miss Mara is his real…?

612
00:26:48,816 --> 00:26:50,067
[Mama M] Mara won't do that!

613
00:26:50,150 --> 00:26:52,110
[Vince] I found out a secret!

614
00:26:52,194 --> 00:26:54,530
- This is insane!
- What secret?

615
00:26:54,613 --> 00:26:56,132
Miss Mara De Jesus
is Angelo's real mother.

616
00:26:56,156 --> 00:26:57,574
- Hey, is that true?
- It's true!

617
00:26:57,658 --> 00:26:58,992
- Oh my God!
- Hey! What's that?

618
00:26:59,076 --> 00:27:00,786
[whispering]

619
00:27:02,371 --> 00:27:03,372
Seriously?

620
00:27:03,455 --> 00:27:04,665
Share it with me.

621
00:27:05,165 --> 00:27:06,500
[whispering]

622
00:27:07,543 --> 00:27:08,585
I didn't hear. Again.

623
00:27:12,089 --> 00:27:13,089
Who?

624
00:27:14,508 --> 00:27:15,884
You're too much.

625
00:27:15,968 --> 00:27:17,636
What are you whispering about?

626
00:27:17,719 --> 00:27:19,263
Oh, Mayet!

627
00:27:19,346 --> 00:27:21,139
You'll faint when you hear this.

628
00:27:21,223 --> 00:27:22,223
What is it?

629
00:27:25,102 --> 00:27:26,895
- Huh?!
- Mayet.

630
00:27:26,979 --> 00:27:30,399
- Mayet, your heart.
- [all] Mayet!

631
00:27:30,482 --> 00:27:32,276
[all] Mayet! Mayet!

632
00:27:32,359 --> 00:27:34,611
- Mayet!
- [Twinkle] My God! What happened?

633
00:27:34,695 --> 00:27:36,071
Mayet! Mayet!

634
00:27:36,154 --> 00:27:37,030
Mayet!

635
00:27:37,114 --> 00:27:39,575
One thousand one,
one thousand two, one thousand three.

636
00:27:39,658 --> 00:27:40,784
Clear!

637
00:27:41,535 --> 00:27:43,036
- What happened?
- Oh my God, sis.

638
00:27:43,120 --> 00:27:44,580
- What?
- We heard some news!

639
00:27:44,663 --> 00:27:46,140
- What is it?
- But you can't tell anyone.

640
00:27:46,164 --> 00:27:47,666
- Tell me.
- Should I?

641
00:27:47,749 --> 00:27:50,085
- Tell me!
- Mayet!

642
00:27:50,168 --> 00:27:52,379
Tell me! What is it?

643
00:27:52,462 --> 00:27:53,714
- I need to know!
- I'm about to!

644
00:27:53,797 --> 00:27:55,424
What is it? Tell me!

645
00:27:55,507 --> 00:27:56,633
- Go tell her!
- What is it?

646
00:27:56,717 --> 00:27:58,218
I'm going to!

647
00:27:58,302 --> 00:27:59,469
Angelo's real mother…

648
00:27:59,553 --> 00:28:00,470
Angelo's real mother

649
00:28:00,554 --> 00:28:03,265
is Mara De Jesus.

650
00:28:05,142 --> 00:28:07,936
Angelo's real mother is Mara De Jesus?

651
00:28:08,020 --> 00:28:09,021
Exactly!

652
00:28:10,522 --> 00:28:11,522
It's true!

653
00:28:11,565 --> 00:28:13,025
How did you find out?

654
00:28:21,909 --> 00:28:23,577
Why is this my fault?

655
00:28:23,660 --> 00:28:25,412
It really is my fault, Mother.

656
00:28:25,495 --> 00:28:26,495
I'm sorry.

657
00:28:26,538 --> 00:28:29,458
I heard you and Mama M
in the kitchen earlier.

658
00:28:29,541 --> 00:28:30,541
You?

659
00:28:32,210 --> 00:28:33,545
So, sis,

660
00:28:34,254 --> 00:28:35,505
is it true

661
00:28:35,589 --> 00:28:37,507
that Mara De Jesus

662
00:28:37,591 --> 00:28:40,761
is Angelo's real mommy?

663
00:28:47,434 --> 00:28:49,102
[gasps of shock]

664
00:28:49,186 --> 00:28:50,395
Oh my God.

665
00:28:50,479 --> 00:28:53,482
So, that means…

666
00:28:54,775 --> 00:28:56,151
We're rich!

667
00:28:56,235 --> 00:28:57,945
[cheering]

668
00:28:58,028 --> 00:28:59,488
We're gonna be rich!

669
00:28:59,571 --> 00:29:01,073
Stop it!

670
00:29:01,698 --> 00:29:02,950
Quiet!

671
00:29:03,033 --> 00:29:04,033
Quiet!

672
00:29:04,952 --> 00:29:08,664
No one can know that Mara De Jesus

673
00:29:08,747 --> 00:29:11,875
is Angelo's real mother!

674
00:29:11,959 --> 00:29:15,295
Go ahead! Scream it
so the whole town hears you.

675
00:29:15,379 --> 00:29:16,588
Should I give you the mic too?

676
00:29:16,672 --> 00:29:18,006
[breathing heavily]

677
00:29:18,090 --> 00:29:23,053
[whispering] No one can know
that Mara De Jesus

678
00:29:23,136 --> 00:29:27,641
is Angelo's real mother.

679
00:29:28,225 --> 00:29:29,393
Absolutely

680
00:29:29,476 --> 00:29:31,311
no one.

681
00:29:31,853 --> 00:29:34,481
Sis, not even Angelo?

682
00:29:34,564 --> 00:29:35,649
Wanna tell him?

683
00:29:35,732 --> 00:29:38,652
- Wanna tell Angelo? Then do it.
- I was just asking.

684
00:29:38,735 --> 00:29:41,113
- Tell Angelo! Tell him.
- [mutters indistinctly]

685
00:29:41,196 --> 00:29:42,364
Mess with the kid's head.

686
00:29:42,447 --> 00:29:44,241
- Tell him. Go ahead.
- Sorry! Sorry.

687
00:29:44,324 --> 00:29:45,450
Make the kid rebel.

688
00:29:45,534 --> 00:29:47,411
Make him run away from me.
Make him reject me.

689
00:29:47,494 --> 00:29:48,578
Tell him! Go ahead!

690
00:29:48,662 --> 00:29:50,539
Try it! Tell Angelo.

691
00:29:51,498 --> 00:29:55,544
I'll swarm your panties with red ants.

692
00:29:55,627 --> 00:29:56,753
[Ria] Ouch! That hurts!

693
00:29:56,837 --> 00:29:58,255
Go ahead.

694
00:29:58,338 --> 00:30:01,133
I'll make sure your privates swell up.

695
00:30:02,009 --> 00:30:03,635
That would hurt.

696
00:30:04,177 --> 00:30:07,848
No one can know until that woman
signs the child over to me.

697
00:30:09,141 --> 00:30:11,143
[kids arguing]

698
00:30:11,226 --> 00:30:12,394
Son!

699
00:30:13,353 --> 00:30:15,689
Is this your son?

700
00:30:15,772 --> 00:30:18,817
- Yes, sir. What's the matter?
- You should talk to him!

701
00:30:18,900 --> 00:30:21,820
He threw spaghetti at his classmate!

702
00:30:21,903 --> 00:30:23,405
Do you see what's going on?

703
00:30:23,488 --> 00:30:26,116
I knew it. Those kids are bullying my son!

704
00:30:26,199 --> 00:30:27,617
I know Angelo.

705
00:30:27,701 --> 00:30:29,995
He would never do anything bad.

706
00:30:30,579 --> 00:30:31,913
Right, son?

707
00:30:31,997 --> 00:30:34,291
Sweetie, what did Mama teach you?

708
00:30:34,374 --> 00:30:37,544
Life is like one big beauty pageant.

709
00:30:37,627 --> 00:30:39,588
It's not about who throws
the strongest punch,

710
00:30:39,671 --> 00:30:41,173
it's about who gives the best answer!

711
00:30:41,256 --> 00:30:42,716
And when your answer is right?

712
00:30:42,799 --> 00:30:44,134
You always win!

713
00:30:44,760 --> 00:30:47,763
Thank you for that wonderful answer!

714
00:30:47,846 --> 00:30:49,973
But still, I will report this

715
00:30:50,057 --> 00:30:52,893
as we do not tolerate violence
in this school.

716
00:30:54,436 --> 00:30:57,439
See? He's sticking his tongue out!
That child is the spawn of a tik-tik.

717
00:31:00,692 --> 00:31:02,110
- Ma.
- What happened?

718
00:31:02,194 --> 00:31:04,696
- They were making fun of me.
- Why?

719
00:31:04,780 --> 00:31:09,659
I said we're moving to Hong Kong
and you'll be working in Disneyland.

720
00:31:09,743 --> 00:31:11,119
- And?
- They didn't believe me.

721
00:31:11,203 --> 00:31:12,037
Why?

722
00:31:12,120 --> 00:31:14,247
They said not only are you gay,

723
00:31:14,331 --> 00:31:15,707
you're a liar too!

724
00:31:15,791 --> 00:31:16,893
They're right about that one.

725
00:31:16,917 --> 00:31:18,877
I really am gay.
Nothing we can do about it.

726
00:31:18,960 --> 00:31:20,295
That's not the point.

727
00:31:20,379 --> 00:31:22,047
I fought them

728
00:31:22,130 --> 00:31:25,175
because I don't like them
calling you a liar!

729
00:31:25,258 --> 00:31:28,387
I know you would never lie to me.

730
00:31:28,470 --> 00:31:31,014
Right? We're going to Disneyland?

731
00:31:31,098 --> 00:31:36,561
[soft music playing]

732
00:31:36,645 --> 00:31:38,939
[school bell rings]

733
00:31:39,022 --> 00:31:45,320
[tense music playing]

734
00:31:51,034 --> 00:31:53,245
Are we going any higher?
My neck is cramping.

735
00:31:54,037 --> 00:31:55,163
Ms. J?

736
00:31:55,664 --> 00:31:56,748
You can drop it.

737
00:32:01,753 --> 00:32:03,004
So?

738
00:32:03,088 --> 00:32:05,340
I'm here because
I'm agreeing to be your coach.

739
00:32:05,424 --> 00:32:06,258
Thank God.

740
00:32:06,341 --> 00:32:07,801
But I have three conditions.

741
00:32:07,884 --> 00:32:09,469
[Ms. J] Excuse me. We agreed on one.

742
00:32:09,553 --> 00:32:10,988
You don't wanna hear it?
Then never mind.

743
00:32:11,012 --> 00:32:11,888
- Bye!
- I'm going home.

744
00:32:11,972 --> 00:32:13,223
What are the conditions?

745
00:32:16,518 --> 00:32:17,686
First,

746
00:32:18,728 --> 00:32:21,314
I resigned from my old job
so I can go full-time for you.

747
00:32:21,398 --> 00:32:23,817
So you need to double my salary.

748
00:32:24,734 --> 00:32:25,735
Sure.

749
00:32:25,819 --> 00:32:26,736
I'll make it four times!

750
00:32:26,820 --> 00:32:27,863
As your assistant,

751
00:32:27,946 --> 00:32:30,532
your bodyguard, and your accountant,
that won't be possible.

752
00:32:30,615 --> 00:32:32,385
Oh, it's not possible?
Then we don't have a deal.

753
00:32:32,409 --> 00:32:33,410
We'll make it possible!

754
00:32:34,494 --> 00:32:37,456
I'll just deduct it from Ms. J's salary.

755
00:32:37,539 --> 00:32:39,166
[Twinkle] There you go.

756
00:32:39,249 --> 00:32:40,167
Perfect!

757
00:32:40,250 --> 00:32:41,418
See? You can manage.

758
00:32:42,169 --> 00:32:43,587
Second,

759
00:32:45,380 --> 00:32:47,757
you need to help with the secret adoption.

760
00:32:48,717 --> 00:32:50,635
You cannot miss the counseling sessions

761
00:32:50,719 --> 00:32:53,597
because it might delay
the filing of the petition.

762
00:32:53,680 --> 00:32:56,224
And you need to sign.

763
00:32:57,267 --> 00:32:58,435
Okay.

764
00:32:58,518 --> 00:33:00,395
Third, and most important:

765
00:33:01,897 --> 00:33:04,107
You can't go near Angelo.

766
00:33:05,692 --> 00:33:07,110
Angelo?

767
00:33:07,194 --> 00:33:08,445
So, do we have a deal?

768
00:33:09,070 --> 00:33:10,113
Game!

769
00:33:18,330 --> 00:33:20,207
Mara, what did we get ourselves into?

770
00:33:20,290 --> 00:33:21,583
Where are we?

771
00:33:22,667 --> 00:33:23,585
Twinkle?

772
00:33:23,668 --> 00:33:24,794
[footsteps approaching]

773
00:33:24,878 --> 00:33:26,379
- What is this?
- Twinkle!

774
00:33:26,463 --> 00:33:30,550
[maniacal laughter]

775
00:33:39,351 --> 00:33:41,853
Mara, a pageant coach wouldn't
pull these parlor tricks.

776
00:33:41,937 --> 00:33:44,147
Twinkle looks more like
a fraternity leader.

777
00:33:44,231 --> 00:33:46,066
- Be quiet!
- Ouch!

778
00:33:46,149 --> 00:33:47,275
Welcome

779
00:33:47,943 --> 00:33:51,071
to my multi-level intensive training camp

780
00:33:51,154 --> 00:33:54,950
exclusively for queens.

781
00:33:55,033 --> 00:33:57,536
Vince. Attack.

782
00:33:57,619 --> 00:33:59,496
- [yells]
- [Mara and Ms. J shriek]

783
00:34:02,916 --> 00:34:06,503
[laughing]

784
00:34:06,586 --> 00:34:08,213
What's so funny?

785
00:34:08,296 --> 00:34:09,339
[Mama M clears throat]

786
00:34:09,839 --> 00:34:11,716
[Twinkle] No cell phones allowed.

787
00:34:11,800 --> 00:34:15,470
You need to focus, focus, focus.

788
00:34:16,054 --> 00:34:17,138
In pageants,

789
00:34:17,222 --> 00:34:19,432
you are required to give your best.

790
00:34:19,516 --> 00:34:22,143
Because if you are not the best,

791
00:34:22,227 --> 00:34:25,355
you are just like the rest.

792
00:34:25,438 --> 00:34:26,438
Got it?

793
00:34:27,065 --> 00:34:28,191
I'm excited!

794
00:34:29,109 --> 00:34:30,694
Just like old times!

795
00:34:34,656 --> 00:34:37,325
- Our first lesson will be...
- My signature walk?

796
00:34:37,409 --> 00:34:39,995
All queens nowadays already have
their own walk, right?

797
00:34:40,078 --> 00:34:41,162
So what's mine?

798
00:34:41,246 --> 00:34:42,414
What's the rush?

799
00:34:42,497 --> 00:34:44,124
We'll get to that.

800
00:34:44,207 --> 00:34:45,207
Too eager, huh?

801
00:34:45,917 --> 00:34:48,628
A signature walk is learned.

802
00:34:48,712 --> 00:34:50,255
It takes hard work.

803
00:34:50,338 --> 00:34:52,591
You need to earn it.

804
00:34:55,844 --> 00:34:57,387
Our first lesson…

805
00:34:57,470 --> 00:34:59,306
- Is balance!
- [light switch clicks]

806
00:34:59,389 --> 00:35:00,890
- And posture!
- [light switch clicks]

807
00:35:00,974 --> 00:35:02,809
[Twinkle] Balance and posture.

808
00:35:02,892 --> 00:35:06,271
These are the two fundamentals
of pageantry.

809
00:35:06,354 --> 00:35:07,772
- Watch me!
- [light switch clicks]

810
00:35:07,856 --> 00:35:12,652
["Reyna" by Michelle Dee playing]

811
00:35:20,619 --> 00:35:22,829
Oh!

812
00:35:23,747 --> 00:35:25,248
Ahh!

813
00:35:25,332 --> 00:35:27,834
- [Mama M] Gorgeous!
- [Vince] You can't pull that off.

814
00:35:27,917 --> 00:35:31,046
- [Mama M] Whoa!
- [Vince] Oh wow!

815
00:35:31,129 --> 00:35:33,465
Oh! Who is he?

816
00:35:33,548 --> 00:35:35,216
[Vince] Yes, yes, yes!

817
00:35:37,302 --> 00:35:38,970
Here comes the turn!

818
00:35:39,054 --> 00:35:42,432
[Vince and Mama M Chuckling]

819
00:35:45,101 --> 00:35:46,686
Your turn.

820
00:35:51,650 --> 00:35:52,942
Go, Mara!

821
00:35:53,026 --> 00:35:54,694
[Ms. J] My queen is fabulous.

822
00:35:55,236 --> 00:35:56,529
Go, Mara!

823
00:35:56,613 --> 00:35:58,198
There! Push!

824
00:35:58,281 --> 00:36:00,075
Sway that hip!

825
00:36:00,158 --> 00:36:01,368
Emote!

826
00:36:01,868 --> 00:36:03,870
That's my queen right there.

827
00:36:05,288 --> 00:36:06,331
Killing it!

828
00:36:06,414 --> 00:36:08,291
Go, Mara! [Claps]

829
00:36:08,375 --> 00:36:10,251
[Ms. J] Well done!

830
00:36:10,877 --> 00:36:11,877
Emote!

831
00:36:14,297 --> 00:36:15,173
Too easy!

832
00:36:15,256 --> 00:36:16,299
[Mama M gasps]

833
00:36:16,383 --> 00:36:17,383
You think so?

834
00:36:17,926 --> 00:36:18,926
Level 2!

835
00:36:19,886 --> 00:36:21,012
[Mara] Seriously?

836
00:36:21,096 --> 00:36:25,558
["Reyna" continues]

837
00:36:25,642 --> 00:36:26,476
Oh!

838
00:36:26,559 --> 00:36:28,728
Wow! Nice! [Claps]

839
00:36:28,812 --> 00:36:30,271
You truly are unbeatable!

840
00:36:30,355 --> 00:36:33,149
Even the goldfish is perfectly balanced!

841
00:36:34,359 --> 00:36:35,610
Wow!

842
00:36:35,694 --> 00:36:36,986
Fishtacular!

843
00:36:37,070 --> 00:36:38,822
[Vince] Wow! [Clapping]

844
00:36:38,905 --> 00:36:40,323
[Mama M] Oh!

845
00:36:40,407 --> 00:36:42,283
Step up or give up?

846
00:36:42,867 --> 00:36:44,703
No freaking way!

847
00:36:45,286 --> 00:36:47,122
I can see you sweating!

848
00:36:47,205 --> 00:36:48,957
The fish swims fast though.

849
00:36:50,125 --> 00:36:52,001
[Ms. J] Mara can do this.
Go, Mara!

850
00:36:52,085 --> 00:36:54,629
- Almost there, Miss Mara!
- Emote!

851
00:36:54,713 --> 00:36:57,841
Careful, it might fall.

852
00:36:57,924 --> 00:36:59,801
- [Mara] Can we take a break?
- No!

853
00:37:00,343 --> 00:37:01,428
Mama!

854
00:37:02,595 --> 00:37:03,680
[Mama M] Oh!

855
00:37:03,763 --> 00:37:06,141
This is my special recipe for chop suey!

856
00:37:06,224 --> 00:37:07,225
Perfect!

857
00:37:07,308 --> 00:37:09,269
What is this, a cooking show?

858
00:37:09,352 --> 00:37:10,895
Careful. It's hot!

859
00:37:10,979 --> 00:37:12,814
Watch and learn.

860
00:37:15,275 --> 00:37:18,570
You are really good.

861
00:37:18,653 --> 00:37:20,613
Let her cook!

862
00:37:23,783 --> 00:37:24,826
Can you do it?

863
00:37:24,909 --> 00:37:26,369
Cheftastic!

864
00:37:27,036 --> 00:37:30,373
- Wow!
- [clapping]

865
00:37:30,457 --> 00:37:33,126
Oh, I thought it was "too easy"?

866
00:37:33,209 --> 00:37:35,170
I know what you're doing, Twinkle.

867
00:37:35,253 --> 00:37:36,838
I will never give in.

868
00:37:37,547 --> 00:37:39,716
No freaking way!

869
00:37:40,300 --> 00:37:41,843
Don't touch it, Mara. It's hot.

870
00:37:41,926 --> 00:37:42,802
Go slow, okay!

871
00:37:42,886 --> 00:37:44,554
It's still steaming, Mara!

872
00:37:44,637 --> 00:37:46,723
[Ms. J] Don't burn your skin.

873
00:37:49,976 --> 00:37:52,479
[Mama M] We'll still eat that later.

874
00:37:53,062 --> 00:37:53,980
You can quit.

875
00:37:54,063 --> 00:37:55,063
Just say it.

876
00:37:56,941 --> 00:37:58,318
- Careful.
- Mara, be careful!

877
00:37:58,401 --> 00:37:59,778
- [screams]
- [clatters]

878
00:37:59,861 --> 00:38:00,779
Mara!

879
00:38:00,862 --> 00:38:02,781
- Oh my God! The chop suey!
- Mara!

880
00:38:02,864 --> 00:38:04,532
[laughs]

881
00:38:05,241 --> 00:38:06,868
Weak.

882
00:38:08,286 --> 00:38:09,871
Can we have a water break?

883
00:38:09,954 --> 00:38:11,915
No freaking way!

884
00:38:13,875 --> 00:38:16,669
Mother, weren't you a little
too hard on Miss Mara?

885
00:38:16,753 --> 00:38:18,004
Too hard on her?

886
00:38:18,087 --> 00:38:19,774
You're the one
who clipped a tamaraw's horns,

887
00:38:19,798 --> 00:38:20,840
and I'm the harsh one?

888
00:38:20,924 --> 00:38:22,759
And doesn't she want to win?

889
00:38:22,842 --> 00:38:24,928
You're a terrifying coach.

890
00:38:25,011 --> 00:38:26,638
Poor girl.

891
00:38:26,721 --> 00:38:27,972
You feel sorry for her?

892
00:38:28,056 --> 00:38:30,642
Feel sorry for your face.
It's been begging for a retouch.

893
00:38:30,725 --> 00:38:32,977
Easy. Feisty even here?

894
00:38:37,065 --> 00:38:38,650
[Ms. J] Is this it, Mara?

895
00:38:39,943 --> 00:38:40,985
The sign.

896
00:38:41,528 --> 00:38:43,071
Bea, where's Angelo?

897
00:38:43,154 --> 00:38:45,865
Oh, he's with Marco
in the next bar an gay, Mother.

898
00:38:46,491 --> 00:38:49,744
They heard there's some kind
of mini Disneyland?

899
00:38:49,828 --> 00:38:50,995
What mini Disneyland?

900
00:38:51,079 --> 00:38:52,497
Mini Disneyland. The fair.

901
00:38:52,580 --> 00:38:53,974
Since when did they have a fair there?

902
00:38:53,998 --> 00:38:54,916
I don't know.

903
00:38:54,999 --> 00:38:56,084
They passed by earlier.

904
00:38:56,167 --> 00:38:57,544
Marco, where's Angelo?

905
00:38:57,627 --> 00:38:58,795
I don't know, Mother.

906
00:38:58,878 --> 00:39:00,797
Didn't you say you were with Angelo?

907
00:39:00,880 --> 00:39:02,674
I couldn't go, remember?
I went to the gym.

908
00:39:02,757 --> 00:39:04,801
Pretty sure Ria went with him.

909
00:39:04,884 --> 00:39:06,678
Mother! Had dinner yet?

910
00:39:07,262 --> 00:39:08,596
Then why is she here?

911
00:39:08,680 --> 00:39:10,557
They said you took Angelo to the fair.

912
00:39:10,640 --> 00:39:13,518
Oh, I didn't go with him.
I had an online class.

913
00:39:14,102 --> 00:39:16,062
Kid, let me see that tablet.

914
00:39:16,145 --> 00:39:19,440
You can't take what isn't yours!

915
00:39:19,524 --> 00:39:20,859
Give it back!

916
00:39:21,651 --> 00:39:22,986
Excuse me.

917
00:39:23,069 --> 00:39:24,487
Give it back to him!

918
00:39:24,571 --> 00:39:25,613
What if I don't want to?

919
00:39:26,197 --> 00:39:27,240
Let's see about that.

920
00:39:28,741 --> 00:39:31,286
Bro, you picked
the wrong kid to mess with.

921
00:39:31,369 --> 00:39:32,579
You'll be sorry.

922
00:39:33,121 --> 00:39:33,955
Give me that!

923
00:39:34,038 --> 00:39:35,206
Hand it over!

924
00:39:37,709 --> 00:39:39,544
Look what you did!

925
00:39:40,336 --> 00:39:41,713
Oh no!

926
00:39:42,380 --> 00:39:44,591
He broke my tablet!

927
00:39:44,674 --> 00:39:47,176
[Mara] Oh, I'm sorry! Please don't cry!

928
00:39:47,802 --> 00:39:50,096
Please don't cry.

929
00:39:50,179 --> 00:39:52,348
[crying continues]

930
00:39:52,432 --> 00:39:55,602
You're starting to piss me off.
Who actually went with Angelo to the fair?

931
00:39:55,685 --> 00:39:57,645
What, he went to the fair alone?

932
00:39:59,230 --> 00:40:01,274
- [crying]
- [Mara makes soothing noises]

933
00:40:02,859 --> 00:40:04,068
[Mara] Sorry.

934
00:40:05,695 --> 00:40:07,363
I'm so sorry.

935
00:40:07,447 --> 00:40:10,199
Stop crying now, please.

936
00:40:10,950 --> 00:40:11,950
What are you doing here?

937
00:40:11,993 --> 00:40:14,495
Angelo, son, why are you crying?
What's wrong?

938
00:40:14,579 --> 00:40:16,873
- [Ms. J] A jerk tried to take his tablet.
- Angelo?

939
00:40:18,708 --> 00:40:21,127
You bastard!
Why are you picking on a child?

940
00:40:21,210 --> 00:40:22,503
He's a kid. He can't fight back.

941
00:40:22,587 --> 00:40:24,464
Face me instead. Face me.

942
00:40:24,547 --> 00:40:26,841
Hey! Why are you pulling out a knife?

943
00:40:26,925 --> 00:40:28,694
We don't need to go that far.
What do you want?

944
00:40:28,718 --> 00:40:30,511
A cell phone?
Here, I have a cell phone.

945
00:40:31,304 --> 00:40:33,139
Who else has a cell phone?
Give it to me.

946
00:40:33,222 --> 00:40:34,933
Here. What else do you need? Money?

947
00:40:35,016 --> 00:40:36,851
I have money.
You don't need to stab anyone.

948
00:40:36,935 --> 00:40:39,562
Come on, give him some money!
Faster, Marco!

949
00:40:39,646 --> 00:40:41,189
No one should bleed!

950
00:40:41,272 --> 00:40:43,524
Food. Feed him. He's hungry.

951
00:40:43,608 --> 00:40:44,817
What do you want?
Here, here.

952
00:40:44,901 --> 00:40:46,503
- Take him home to your mom!
- I don't want that!

953
00:40:46,527 --> 00:40:47,362
You don't want to?

954
00:40:47,445 --> 00:40:50,114
Come back at Christmas
if you need more, okay?

955
00:40:50,198 --> 00:40:52,158
- [gasps]
- Oh my!

956
00:40:52,241 --> 00:40:55,536
[Angelo continues crying]

957
00:40:56,371 --> 00:40:58,790
- We'll just replace your tablet, okay?
- It's Miss Mara!

958
00:40:58,873 --> 00:41:01,542
- Don't cry. Okay?
- Oh my!

959
00:41:01,626 --> 00:41:03,336
- Okay.
- [onlookers] It's Miss Mara!

960
00:41:03,419 --> 00:41:06,464
- It's Miss Mara!
- It's Miss Mara!

961
00:41:06,547 --> 00:41:08,174
[Angelo] You're famous, right?

962
00:41:08,257 --> 00:41:09,384
Cool!

963
00:41:09,467 --> 00:41:11,761
My guardian angel is famous!

964
00:41:13,721 --> 00:41:16,307
Marco, bring the child inside.

965
00:41:17,684 --> 00:41:18,685
[Bea] Hello, Miss Mara!

966
00:41:18,768 --> 00:41:20,204
- You're so beautiful in person!
- Hello.

967
00:41:20,228 --> 00:41:21,229
Go inside.

968
00:41:25,900 --> 00:41:27,402
What are you doing here?

969
00:41:27,485 --> 00:41:28,736
Didn't I tell you

970
00:41:28,820 --> 00:41:30,738
that you can't see the child?

971
00:41:30,822 --> 00:41:34,033
Uh, I came here because
you didn't return our phones.

972
00:41:34,117 --> 00:41:35,118
What phones?

973
00:41:35,618 --> 00:41:36,703
Cell phone?

974
00:41:36,786 --> 00:41:38,538
I forgot to take them out of my pocket.

975
00:41:38,621 --> 00:41:40,081
Sorry. Here, Miss Mara.

976
00:41:40,164 --> 00:41:41,290
- Thank you.
- Here, Ms. J.

977
00:41:42,166 --> 00:41:43,501
You got your phones.

978
00:41:43,584 --> 00:41:44,585
Now leave.

979
00:41:47,755 --> 00:41:50,174
Get in the car, come on!

980
00:41:53,052 --> 00:41:54,262
[gate slams]

981
00:41:57,390 --> 00:41:59,142
[Ms. J] Tell me the truth.

982
00:42:00,393 --> 00:42:03,271
Why are you even joining Miss Uniworld?

983
00:42:03,354 --> 00:42:05,023
To win the crown?

984
00:42:05,106 --> 00:42:07,859
Or to get close to Twinkle and the child?

985
00:42:09,193 --> 00:42:10,236
You know,

986
00:42:10,319 --> 00:42:13,281
joining the pageant
has always been my dream.

987
00:42:14,032 --> 00:42:16,117
Not because Mama wants me to,

988
00:42:16,200 --> 00:42:18,661
but because I really want it too.

989
00:42:19,537 --> 00:42:21,748
I want to redeem myself.

990
00:42:21,831 --> 00:42:23,249
But at the same time,

991
00:42:24,125 --> 00:42:26,461
I can't get Angelo out of my mind.

992
00:42:27,003 --> 00:42:28,588
Exactly.

993
00:42:28,671 --> 00:42:30,089
It's making me nervous.

994
00:42:30,173 --> 00:42:31,799
What if Anton finds out?

995
00:42:31,883 --> 00:42:33,134
Ms. J,

996
00:42:33,217 --> 00:42:35,845
when Anton and I get married,
we'll be living in the US.

997
00:42:35,928 --> 00:42:37,263
That's what he wants.

998
00:42:38,514 --> 00:42:41,934
This is my last chance
to get to know my son.

999
00:42:44,312 --> 00:42:48,066
I've spent so many years
wondering who he is

1000
00:42:48,858 --> 00:42:50,610
or what he looks like.

1001
00:42:51,360 --> 00:42:53,738
Do you know what that feels like?

1002
00:42:57,909 --> 00:43:00,787
I want to hold him
just to see how it feels.

1003
00:43:01,662 --> 00:43:04,540
And if working with Twinkle
is the only way to do that,

1004
00:43:04,624 --> 00:43:06,125
then I'll do it.

1005
00:43:10,630 --> 00:43:14,175
- [footsteps approaching]
- [light switch clicks]

1006
00:43:14,258 --> 00:43:17,386
Now of all days I forget my umbrella.

1007
00:43:18,721 --> 00:43:19,764
[exhales loudly]

1008
00:43:27,814 --> 00:43:29,023
I have a change of clothes.

1009
00:43:36,322 --> 00:43:37,573
Twinkle?

1010
00:43:41,410 --> 00:43:42,410
You're late!

1011
00:43:42,453 --> 00:43:44,997
What's my number one rule?

1012
00:43:45,081 --> 00:43:48,209
On time is late, and late is unacceptable.

1013
00:43:49,085 --> 00:43:50,670
[Mara] I'm sorry. It's pouring outside.

1014
00:43:50,753 --> 00:43:51,796
Traffic was awful.

1015
00:43:53,464 --> 00:43:56,300
- How did you get that scar?
- [thunder rumbling]

1016
00:43:57,510 --> 00:43:58,719
My scar?

1017
00:43:59,762 --> 00:44:01,931
That's where Angelo came out
when I had him.

1018
00:44:02,014 --> 00:44:03,617
- Cesarean section.
- [electricity crackles]

1019
00:44:03,641 --> 00:44:04,725
[cell phone chimes]

1020
00:44:04,809 --> 00:44:06,686
[thunder rumbles]

1021
00:44:06,769 --> 00:44:07,687
Oh no.

1022
00:44:07,770 --> 00:44:09,647
There's flooding from the heavy rain.

1023
00:44:09,730 --> 00:44:12,650
Start warming up.
I just have to make a call.

1024
00:44:16,279 --> 00:44:17,822
[line ringing]

1025
00:44:17,905 --> 00:44:19,240
Hello, Mayet?

1026
00:44:19,323 --> 00:44:20,616
Have you picked up Angelo?

1027
00:44:20,700 --> 00:44:22,451
[Mayet] <i>What time is it?</i>

1028
00:44:23,077 --> 00:44:25,371
So he's still at school?

1029
00:44:25,454 --> 00:44:28,374
<i>Sorry, sis. I got distracted.
But I'm leaving now.</i>

1030
00:44:28,457 --> 00:44:30,418
Never mind. You're unbelievable.

1031
00:44:32,795 --> 00:44:34,839
Is it okay
if we postpone today's training?

1032
00:44:34,922 --> 00:44:35,798
Yeah, it's okay.

1033
00:44:35,882 --> 00:44:37,675
Let's just pick up Angelo.

1034
00:44:39,719 --> 00:44:41,137
No, it's okay. I've got this.

1035
00:44:41,220 --> 00:44:43,723
Don't turn down my offer.

1036
00:44:43,806 --> 00:44:45,516
A wise mama once said,

1037
00:44:45,600 --> 00:44:48,311
a mother who loves her child
will set her pride aside.

1038
00:44:50,187 --> 00:44:52,356
And a wise philosopher once said,

1039
00:44:53,149 --> 00:44:55,002
less talking, more doing!
What are we waiting for?

1040
00:44:55,026 --> 00:44:57,612
Here. I have the keys. I'll drive.

1041
00:44:58,863 --> 00:45:00,197
Hurry!

1042
00:45:00,281 --> 00:45:04,452
- [rain pouring]
- [thunder rumbling]

1043
00:45:11,334 --> 00:45:12,960
Why did you lend me a broken umbrella?

1044
00:45:13,044 --> 00:45:14,044
[Angelo] Mama!

1045
00:45:15,296 --> 00:45:17,377
- Sweetie, stay right there.
- [motorcycle engine revs]

1046
00:45:17,423 --> 00:45:19,300
Hey! You're so rude!

1047
00:45:19,383 --> 00:45:21,552
I took forever to get ready,
and you just soak me?

1048
00:45:21,636 --> 00:45:23,679
Hey! How dare you?!

1049
00:45:23,763 --> 00:45:25,014
There he is!

1050
00:45:25,097 --> 00:45:26,724
I'm drenched!

1051
00:45:27,516 --> 00:45:28,809
The rain stopped.

1052
00:45:30,311 --> 00:45:32,480
- Hi, Miss Mara!
- [Mara] Hi, Angelo!

1053
00:45:34,774 --> 00:45:35,774
Sweetie.

1054
00:45:36,442 --> 00:45:37,693
Are you okay?

1055
00:45:37,777 --> 00:45:38,777
Yes, Ma.

1056
00:45:39,362 --> 00:45:41,739
I actually wanted to play in the rain,

1057
00:45:41,822 --> 00:45:44,492
but it stopped.

1058
00:45:44,575 --> 00:45:46,285
Good thing it did.

1059
00:45:46,369 --> 00:45:47,495
[thunder rumbles]

1060
00:45:47,578 --> 00:45:49,538
[rain pouring]

1061
00:45:49,622 --> 00:45:52,500
My gosh! The weather is so crazy.

1062
00:45:52,583 --> 00:45:54,919
Ma, can I play in the rain?

1063
00:45:55,002 --> 00:45:56,587
Oh no, sweetie, don't.

1064
00:45:56,671 --> 00:45:58,756
You'll catch a cold. You might get sick.

1065
00:45:58,839 --> 00:46:01,634
- But my guardian angel is here!
- Maybe next time.

1066
00:46:01,717 --> 00:46:03,219
Come on, Angelo!

1067
00:46:03,886 --> 00:46:05,304
- Angelo!
- [Mara shrieks]

1068
00:46:05,388 --> 00:46:07,264
[chuckles]

1069
00:46:07,348 --> 00:46:08,468
[Twinkle] Control your girl!

1070
00:46:08,516 --> 00:46:09,892
Or I'll drown you in the gutter!

1071
00:46:09,976 --> 00:46:11,227
[Ms. J] Sorry, sis.

1072
00:46:11,310 --> 00:46:13,521
Playing in the rain is kind of our hobby.

1073
00:46:13,604 --> 00:46:14,897
What are you doing?

1074
00:46:15,731 --> 00:46:17,108
Ma, come join us!

1075
00:46:17,191 --> 00:46:19,402
We're in the school grounds!

1076
00:46:19,485 --> 00:46:20,485
Angelo!

1077
00:46:21,404 --> 00:46:23,698
Son! You might get sick!

1078
00:46:23,781 --> 00:46:25,241
No! Come on, Ma!

1079
00:46:25,324 --> 00:46:26,575
Join us, Ma!

1080
00:46:27,827 --> 00:46:29,578
- Son!
- [Mara] Catch him!

1081
00:46:29,662 --> 00:46:32,665
I'm glad we're doing this after all!
This is so fun!

1082
00:46:32,748 --> 00:46:36,002
I told you to control your girl.
Sweetie, this is so fun!

1083
00:46:36,085 --> 00:46:38,754
Thank goodness you thought of this.

1084
00:46:40,506 --> 00:46:43,592
Here's the snack you asked for!

1085
00:46:43,676 --> 00:46:45,928
- [Vince] Thank you so much, Mayet!
- [Mayet] That's yummy!

1086
00:46:46,929 --> 00:46:48,931
Hey, guys!

1087
00:46:49,015 --> 00:46:51,517
I brought my guardian angel with me.

1088
00:46:51,600 --> 00:46:54,478
My guardian angel, Miss Mara!

1089
00:46:54,562 --> 00:46:58,649
Miss Mara's car broke down,
so they're staying here for now.

1090
00:47:00,067 --> 00:47:02,170
But she won't be staying long.
She's leaving soon, right?

1091
00:47:02,194 --> 00:47:05,406
She still has a shoot for a movie.

1092
00:47:05,489 --> 00:47:07,742
Ah, yes, sorry for the trouble.

1093
00:47:07,825 --> 00:47:11,078
Ms. J already called to get our car fixed.

1094
00:47:11,162 --> 00:47:13,831
- So as soon as it's done...
- No, Miss Mara.

1095
00:47:13,914 --> 00:47:15,634
You can stay here
for as long as you'd like.

1096
00:47:15,708 --> 00:47:16,792
- Just stay here.
- Yes.

1097
00:47:16,876 --> 00:47:18,437
[Ria] And we have an extra bed
in our room.

1098
00:47:18,461 --> 00:47:20,731
- You can spend the night here.
- [Bea] And we've just made some snacks!

1099
00:47:20,755 --> 00:47:23,007
- Perfect timing!
- Wow!

1100
00:47:23,090 --> 00:47:25,968
Aren't you just the best hosts.

1101
00:47:26,052 --> 00:47:27,178
You too.

1102
00:47:27,261 --> 00:47:28,721
What a sweet gesture!

1103
00:47:28,804 --> 00:47:30,139
Overnight?

1104
00:47:30,222 --> 00:47:32,767
You're not even paying rent,
and yet you invite someone over!

1105
00:47:32,850 --> 00:47:34,935
You think you own this house?

1106
00:47:35,478 --> 00:47:37,730
- You're all shameless.
- Your towel.

1107
00:47:38,439 --> 00:47:40,232
[Mayet] I'll give Angelo a bath first.

1108
00:47:40,316 --> 00:47:44,111
Wait. I want to show
my paintings to Miss Mara.

1109
00:47:45,154 --> 00:47:47,406
Sure! Show me.

1110
00:47:47,490 --> 00:47:50,201
These are all my paintings.

1111
00:47:50,284 --> 00:47:51,327
[Mara] Amazing!

1112
00:47:51,410 --> 00:47:53,245
- You did all of these?
- [Angelo] Yes.

1113
00:47:53,329 --> 00:47:54,747
You're really good at painting.

1114
00:47:54,830 --> 00:47:57,625
Mayet, the kid needs a bath now.

1115
00:47:58,334 --> 00:48:00,419
Come on.

1116
00:48:00,503 --> 00:48:06,425
[soft music playing]

1117
00:48:09,595 --> 00:48:11,305
Sweetie, eat up.

1118
00:48:11,388 --> 00:48:12,473
Open wide.

1119
00:48:12,556 --> 00:48:14,433
I don't like shrimp, Ma!

1120
00:48:15,351 --> 00:48:17,019
I don't like shrimps either.

1121
00:48:17,103 --> 00:48:19,146
- [Bea] Aww, how cute!
- We're the same.

1122
00:48:19,230 --> 00:48:20,481
They're alike!

1123
00:48:20,564 --> 00:48:22,191
[gushing]

1124
00:48:22,274 --> 00:48:23,526
- Mayet?
- Yes, Mother?

1125
00:48:23,609 --> 00:48:26,529
I told you not to put shrimp
in the noodles.

1126
00:48:26,612 --> 00:48:28,864
- You know I'm allergic to this, right?
- [Mayet] Huh?

1127
00:48:28,948 --> 00:48:30,407
Since when?

1128
00:48:30,491 --> 00:48:33,452
You love eating the prawn heads!

1129
00:48:33,536 --> 00:48:36,539
I was diagnosed yesterday.
I'm allergic today.

1130
00:48:38,666 --> 00:48:39,917
[Angelo and Mara sneezing]

1131
00:48:40,501 --> 00:48:41,418
Sorry, um,

1132
00:48:41,502 --> 00:48:43,045
I'm allergic to scents.

1133
00:48:43,129 --> 00:48:46,841
- [Bea] Wow! They're so alike!
- Seriously!

1134
00:48:46,924 --> 00:48:48,300
[breathing heavily]

1135
00:48:48,384 --> 00:48:50,094
Mother? What's wrong, Mother?

1136
00:48:50,177 --> 00:48:51,345
[coughing]

1137
00:48:51,428 --> 00:48:54,932
Did you put on perfume?
I'm allergic to scents!

1138
00:48:55,015 --> 00:48:56,934
[coughing]

1139
00:48:57,017 --> 00:49:00,896
But don't you have a collection
of scented candles, Mother?

1140
00:49:00,980 --> 00:49:02,815
[breathing heavily]

1141
00:49:02,898 --> 00:49:04,942
Mara, try this on your noodles.

1142
00:49:05,025 --> 00:49:06,485
I don't like that.

1143
00:49:06,569 --> 00:49:07,695
Ah, right.

1144
00:49:07,778 --> 00:49:09,405
You don't like sour garnish.

1145
00:49:09,488 --> 00:49:10,656
Me neither!

1146
00:49:10,739 --> 00:49:12,158
[Marco] Wow!

1147
00:49:12,241 --> 00:49:13,784
Same again?

1148
00:49:13,868 --> 00:49:17,163
- [Mayet] Exactly the same!
- [Ria] Exactly the same!

1149
00:49:17,830 --> 00:49:18,831
- [bones crack]
- [groaning]

1150
00:49:18,914 --> 00:49:21,625
[friends, Angelo] Mother! Mother!

1151
00:49:22,376 --> 00:49:24,336
- Mother!
- Oh my!

1152
00:49:24,420 --> 00:49:27,047
Did you put a sour garnish on my noodles?

1153
00:49:27,131 --> 00:49:29,008
I'm allergic to sour food!

1154
00:49:29,091 --> 00:49:31,844
Mother! Are you okay?

1155
00:49:32,469 --> 00:49:34,013
There's no point hiding it.

1156
00:49:34,096 --> 00:49:36,324
Angelo and I have so much in common
because I'm his real...

1157
00:49:36,348 --> 00:49:37,348
No!

1158
00:49:38,809 --> 00:49:39,643
I am!

1159
00:49:39,727 --> 00:49:41,729
I'm Angelo's mother!

1160
00:49:45,774 --> 00:49:47,568
[Ms. J] Twinkle, what are you doing?

1161
00:49:47,651 --> 00:49:49,945
I'm only asking for a slice
of that sticky rice.

1162
00:49:50,029 --> 00:49:51,322
Twinkle!

1163
00:49:51,405 --> 00:49:52,405
Huh?

1164
00:49:53,073 --> 00:49:54,450
Ah, thing is,

1165
00:49:54,533 --> 00:49:57,411
it's better if you mix the toasted coconut
with the sticky rice.

1166
00:49:57,494 --> 00:49:58,494
Wanna taste it?

1167
00:49:59,788 --> 00:50:03,959
[cell phone ringing]

1168
00:50:04,043 --> 00:50:05,628
Hello, Dorothy?

1169
00:50:05,711 --> 00:50:08,130
[Dorothy] <i>Twinkle!</i>
<i>You got accepted in Hong Kong!</i>

1170
00:50:08,214 --> 00:50:10,174
<i>They also said you could bring your son!</i>

1171
00:50:10,257 --> 00:50:11,508
<i>- Congrats!</i>
- Huh?

1172
00:50:13,552 --> 00:50:14,552
Son…

1173
00:50:15,930 --> 00:50:17,640
I got accepted in Hong Kong!

1174
00:50:17,723 --> 00:50:19,850
- Yay! I'm going with you, Mama!
- [cheering]

1175
00:50:19,934 --> 00:50:22,645
I got accepted in Hong Kong!

1176
00:50:22,728 --> 00:50:24,855
We're going to Disneyland!

1177
00:50:24,939 --> 00:50:27,024
Yes!

1178
00:50:27,107 --> 00:50:28,400
[Twinkle] We're leaving!

1179
00:50:28,484 --> 00:50:29,818
You should leave too!

1180
00:50:29,902 --> 00:50:32,071
[chuckles]
We're leaving for Hong Kong!

1181
00:50:32,154 --> 00:50:33,405
[Twinkle] Yes!

1182
00:50:33,489 --> 00:50:35,783
You should leave! 'Cause we are!

1183
00:50:35,866 --> 00:50:38,077
[Mara] <i>I know I have to let go,</i>

1184
00:50:38,911 --> 00:50:41,330
<i>but why do I feel this way?</i>

1185
00:50:45,709 --> 00:50:49,463
TWINKLE: ON OUR WAY TO A NEW CHAPTER
IN HONG KONG! THANK YOU, LORD!

1186
00:50:49,546 --> 00:50:53,092
[sobbing]

1187
00:51:04,270 --> 00:51:05,688
[lawyer] Miss De Jesus,

1188
00:51:05,771 --> 00:51:07,690
this is Atty. Esteban.

1189
00:51:07,773 --> 00:51:10,734
He's going to be our witness today.

1190
00:51:10,818 --> 00:51:12,319
And before we proceed,

1191
00:51:12,403 --> 00:51:16,240
I just want to make sure that
we are on the same page.

1192
00:51:16,323 --> 00:51:17,866
Yes, page 2, right?

1193
00:51:17,950 --> 00:51:19,159
There, page 2.

1194
00:51:19,243 --> 00:51:21,704
[lawyer] Miss, I'm talking to Mara.

1195
00:51:22,288 --> 00:51:23,163
Um,

1196
00:51:23,247 --> 00:51:25,040
if you sign this paper,

1197
00:51:25,124 --> 00:51:31,005
it means you give up all rights, duties,

1198
00:51:31,088 --> 00:51:32,965
and connection to the child.

1199
00:51:33,048 --> 00:51:38,470
You willingly give custody
of the child to someone else.

1200
00:51:39,179 --> 00:51:41,390
Are you sure about this?

1201
00:52:01,201 --> 00:52:02,202
Mara.

1202
00:52:02,703 --> 00:52:03,579
Oh, Twinkle.

1203
00:52:03,662 --> 00:52:05,414
I'm so glad you made it.

1204
00:52:05,497 --> 00:52:08,250
- Um, I got you your usual.
- I don't drink anymore.

1205
00:52:08,334 --> 00:52:10,210
But we're celebrating.

1206
00:52:10,294 --> 00:52:13,047
What are we celebrating?
What's the occasion?

1207
00:52:14,173 --> 00:52:16,383
Well, I'm glad you're here.

1208
00:52:17,426 --> 00:52:20,012
I've had something on my mind all day.

1209
00:52:20,095 --> 00:52:22,473
I know only you can answer it.

1210
00:52:23,599 --> 00:52:26,769
But what is the essence of motherhood?

1211
00:52:26,852 --> 00:52:28,145
What?

1212
00:52:28,979 --> 00:52:30,981
I know you have all
the pageant-worthy answers!

1213
00:52:31,065 --> 00:52:32,107
What is the essence of...

1214
00:52:32,191 --> 00:52:34,610
The essence of motherhood
is not about biology.

1215
00:52:35,194 --> 00:52:38,489
It's an act of radical, selfless love.

1216
00:52:38,572 --> 00:52:42,493
It's a choice to nurture, to guide,

1217
00:52:42,576 --> 00:52:44,912
to empower another human being

1218
00:52:44,995 --> 00:52:47,539
to become the best version of themselves.

1219
00:52:47,623 --> 00:52:49,124
And often,

1220
00:52:49,208 --> 00:52:51,668
it requires sacrificing
a piece of yourself.

1221
00:52:54,046 --> 00:52:55,172
And I

1222
00:52:55,255 --> 00:52:56,507
thank you!

1223
00:52:57,049 --> 00:52:58,258
I nailed that!

1224
00:52:58,342 --> 00:53:00,094
It's my turn to ask.

1225
00:53:00,177 --> 00:53:03,097
Okay, Miss Mara De Jesus,
this is the moment.

1226
00:53:03,180 --> 00:53:04,180
Okay.

1227
00:53:04,807 --> 00:53:08,310
The question standing between
you and the crown is this.

1228
00:53:09,937 --> 00:53:11,688
So, listen up, yo.

1229
00:53:12,481 --> 00:53:13,690
[Mara chuckles]

1230
00:53:13,774 --> 00:53:14,983
Mara.

1231
00:53:17,152 --> 00:53:21,490
Every crown demands a sacrifice.

1232
00:53:23,617 --> 00:53:26,412
If the price of your ultimate goal

1233
00:53:27,830 --> 00:53:32,960
is walking away from the person
that you are meant to protect,

1234
00:53:34,336 --> 00:53:38,006
then what does that say about
the queen you aspire to be?

1235
00:53:44,221 --> 00:53:45,222
It's been a long night.

1236
00:53:45,305 --> 00:53:47,266
Deal with it tomorrow.

1237
00:53:47,349 --> 00:53:49,435
Let's practice some other time.

1238
00:53:49,518 --> 00:53:51,603
Thank you for that question.

1239
00:53:55,190 --> 00:53:56,608
It is implied…

1240
00:53:57,317 --> 00:54:00,362
<i>That walking away
is an act of selfishness,</i>

1241
00:54:00,988 --> 00:54:04,491
<i>but I believe that this true sacrifice</i>

1242
00:54:04,575 --> 00:54:06,243
<i>is an act of profound love.</i>

1243
00:54:08,787 --> 00:54:11,832
<i>I, too, walked away from someone
who needed me most.</i>

1244
00:54:11,915 --> 00:54:14,126
<i>Not for the crown,</i>

1245
00:54:14,209 --> 00:54:16,628
<i>but because I wasn't strong enough then.</i>

1246
00:54:21,592 --> 00:54:26,930
The queen I aspire to be is not perfect,

1247
00:54:28,015 --> 00:54:30,142
but one who is honest.

1248
00:54:32,394 --> 00:54:33,604
Thank you.

1249
00:54:39,902 --> 00:54:41,069
What's up with you?

1250
00:54:41,153 --> 00:54:42,863
I thought we were celebrating.

1251
00:54:42,946 --> 00:54:44,239
This is too dramatic.

1252
00:54:44,823 --> 00:54:46,742
Why are we here?

1253
00:54:47,409 --> 00:54:48,494
Well,

1254
00:54:49,036 --> 00:54:51,079
I just wanted to make it up to you.

1255
00:54:52,247 --> 00:54:54,416
I have good news for you, Twinkle.

1256
00:54:55,792 --> 00:54:58,253
I signed the adoption papers.

1257
00:55:00,130 --> 00:55:01,256
For real?

1258
00:55:02,508 --> 00:55:03,800
Oh my God!

1259
00:55:06,386 --> 00:55:08,013
Let's have a toast!

1260
00:55:09,848 --> 00:55:10,848
[glasses clink]

1261
00:55:12,226 --> 00:55:13,226
[Twinkle] <i>Hello, Mutya.</i>

1262
00:55:13,268 --> 00:55:16,063
<i>Mara has signed the adoption papers.
Is there any update?</i>

1263
00:55:16,647 --> 00:55:21,485
[Mutya] <i>I can drop by this week</i>
<i>so Angelo can prepare his written consent.</i>

1264
00:55:21,568 --> 00:55:24,905
After that, we can file the petition.

1265
00:55:26,114 --> 00:55:27,407
Thank God.

1266
00:55:28,325 --> 00:55:29,785
Thank you.

1267
00:55:31,828 --> 00:55:32,996
[Angelo] Thank you, Mama!

1268
00:55:33,080 --> 00:55:35,541
We brought Miss Mara on the field trip!

1269
00:55:35,624 --> 00:55:40,671
[bright music playing]

1270
00:55:40,754 --> 00:55:42,982
[photographer] Excuse me.
All the mommies, gather 'round.

1271
00:55:43,006 --> 00:55:44,967
Let's take a group picture.

1272
00:55:45,884 --> 00:55:47,678
Twinkle, why don't you join?

1273
00:55:47,761 --> 00:55:49,221
No, thanks.

1274
00:55:50,347 --> 00:55:52,307
[photographer]
Here we go, all the mommies!

1275
00:55:52,975 --> 00:55:54,285
- [photographer] Okay.
- [Mara] Sir!

1276
00:55:54,309 --> 00:55:55,561
Hang on.

1277
00:55:55,644 --> 00:55:57,729
Come on, Twinkle. Join them!

1278
00:55:57,813 --> 00:55:59,147
Why?

1279
00:56:00,023 --> 00:56:01,775
He's Angelo's mom.

1280
00:56:01,858 --> 00:56:03,068
[photographer] Come on, Mommy!

1281
00:56:03,151 --> 00:56:04,319
Okay.

1282
00:56:05,112 --> 00:56:06,446
Let's squeeze in.

1283
00:56:06,530 --> 00:56:07,864
And pose.

1284
00:56:07,948 --> 00:56:09,658
- Smile!
- Smile, Mommies!

1285
00:56:09,741 --> 00:56:10,576
Get closer!

1286
00:56:10,659 --> 00:56:13,662
Excuse me.
What's with these lame poses?

1287
00:56:13,745 --> 00:56:15,831
You look like miserable mothers!

1288
00:56:15,914 --> 00:56:17,583
Okay, project. Chin up!

1289
00:56:17,666 --> 00:56:19,126
Chest out!

1290
00:56:19,710 --> 00:56:21,503
Everybody say: Okurr!

1291
00:56:21,587 --> 00:56:23,046
- Okurr!
- Okurr!

1292
00:56:23,130 --> 00:56:24,756
- [photographer] Nice.
- Okurr!

1293
00:56:24,840 --> 00:56:27,676
Twinkle! They're mommies.

1294
00:56:28,969 --> 00:56:30,262
[photographer] Okay.

1295
00:56:30,345 --> 00:56:32,639
- All right. And… smile!
- [camera clicks]

1296
00:56:32,723 --> 00:56:34,492
- [photographer] Yeah, nice.
- [mouths] Thank you.

1297
00:56:34,516 --> 00:56:36,236
- Okay, pose. Pose, Mommies!
- [camera clicks]

1298
00:56:36,935 --> 00:56:39,938
- [photographer] That's it.
- [camera clicks]

1299
00:56:45,444 --> 00:56:47,946
Angelo, can I see your paintbrush?

1300
00:56:48,030 --> 00:56:49,865
Is this still good?

1301
00:56:49,948 --> 00:56:52,743
Ma, I need more water.

1302
00:56:53,702 --> 00:56:55,912
Okay, let me fill your cup.

1303
00:57:00,375 --> 00:57:01,418
Angelo,

1304
00:57:02,669 --> 00:57:04,046
next time we meet,

1305
00:57:04,129 --> 00:57:06,381
I'll buy you some new paintbrushes, okay?

1306
00:57:06,465 --> 00:57:08,425
So you'll have new ones to use.

1307
00:57:08,508 --> 00:57:10,010
No need, Miss Mara.

1308
00:57:10,093 --> 00:57:11,428
This is my favorite.

1309
00:57:11,511 --> 00:57:14,473
I color better with this one.

1310
00:57:15,223 --> 00:57:16,224
What about you?

1311
00:57:16,767 --> 00:57:18,810
Do you have a favorite object?

1312
00:57:19,519 --> 00:57:20,896
I do.

1313
00:57:20,979 --> 00:57:23,774
It's a remembrance
of the most important person

1314
00:57:23,857 --> 00:57:25,150
in the whole world.

1315
00:57:25,233 --> 00:57:28,737
It's the only thing he left behind.

1316
00:57:29,237 --> 00:57:31,406
That's why I take good care of it.

1317
00:57:31,490 --> 00:57:33,075
He left?

1318
00:57:33,659 --> 00:57:35,535
Something like that.

1319
00:57:36,870 --> 00:57:38,997
I let him go.

1320
00:57:40,082 --> 00:57:44,962
But it's okay,
because we met each other again.

1321
00:57:45,045 --> 00:57:46,505
Really?

1322
00:57:46,588 --> 00:57:47,673
Mm-hmm.

1323
00:57:49,257 --> 00:57:51,802
I really want to make it up to him.

1324
00:57:53,762 --> 00:57:56,723
I want to make things right, Angelo.

1325
00:57:56,807 --> 00:58:00,310
[soft music playing]

1326
00:58:00,394 --> 00:58:01,520
[Twinkle] Sweetie!

1327
00:58:01,603 --> 00:58:02,980
Time to fly a kite!

1328
00:58:03,063 --> 00:58:04,815
Come on, get that done.

1329
00:58:06,733 --> 00:58:07,901
Wow!

1330
00:58:08,485 --> 00:58:09,945
That's beautiful!

1331
00:58:10,028 --> 00:58:11,822
- Is it abstract?
- [chuckles]

1332
00:58:11,905 --> 00:58:13,573
This one's me.

1333
00:58:13,657 --> 00:58:15,951
And this is you.

1334
00:58:16,034 --> 00:58:18,537
This is you, Miss Mara.

1335
00:58:25,711 --> 00:58:27,462
Oh, sorry.

1336
00:58:28,714 --> 00:58:29,756
It's okay.

1337
00:58:30,799 --> 00:58:33,593
Oh, sorry.

1338
00:58:36,054 --> 00:58:37,139
You wanna play?

1339
00:58:37,723 --> 00:58:38,932
[chuckles]

1340
00:58:40,600 --> 00:58:42,811
- You wanna join in too?
- [chuckles]

1341
00:58:42,894 --> 00:58:48,400
[upbeat music playing]

1342
00:58:54,072 --> 00:58:55,365
[Angelo laughing]

1343
00:58:59,036 --> 00:59:00,537
Pull it, sweetie.

1344
00:59:00,620 --> 00:59:01,997
It's so high!

1345
00:59:02,080 --> 00:59:02,956
So high!

1346
00:59:03,040 --> 00:59:05,459
Wow, Angelo!

1347
00:59:05,542 --> 00:59:08,086
Your kite is flying so high!

1348
00:59:08,879 --> 00:59:11,882
- Mm!
- Come on, let's fly a kite too.

1349
00:59:14,384 --> 00:59:15,761
Thank you, Mama.

1350
00:59:16,386 --> 00:59:18,263
Thank you, Miss Mara.

1351
00:59:20,307 --> 00:59:23,935
Ma, can Miss Mara come to my birthday?

1352
00:59:26,396 --> 00:59:27,731
Uh…

1353
00:59:27,814 --> 00:59:29,983
Of course, if she's not busy.

1354
00:59:30,067 --> 00:59:31,401
Oh! Oh!

1355
00:59:32,027 --> 00:59:33,487
Thank you, Twinkle.

1356
00:59:34,154 --> 00:59:35,238
[soft laugh]

1357
00:59:35,822 --> 00:59:37,657
[Twinkle] Oh, look.

1358
00:59:40,619 --> 00:59:42,996
[Twinkle]<i> We're done</i>
<i>with the games and challenges.</i>

1359
00:59:43,080 --> 00:59:46,374
Honestly, I have to say, you're good.

1360
00:59:46,458 --> 00:59:48,752
I can see how determined you are to win.

1361
00:59:48,835 --> 00:59:50,295
But who are you, really?

1362
00:59:50,921 --> 00:59:53,381
People need to know who you are

1363
00:59:53,465 --> 00:59:56,009
and why you should win.

1364
00:59:56,593 --> 00:59:59,346
Okay. So, how do we do it?

1365
00:59:59,429 --> 01:00:02,057
You've been pestering me
about your signature walk.

1366
01:00:03,183 --> 01:00:04,684
As your coach,

1367
01:00:04,768 --> 01:00:06,895
I can help you polish it.

1368
01:00:06,978 --> 01:00:08,772
But the idea has to come from you,

1369
01:00:08,855 --> 01:00:11,233
what your signature walk really is.

1370
01:00:14,903 --> 01:00:16,780
[Mara] <i>I don't have a signature walk.</i>

1371
01:00:19,032 --> 01:00:21,159
<i>I don't even know how to tell my story.</i>

1372
01:00:22,244 --> 01:00:24,204
I gave birth, but I wasn't
really a mother per se.

1373
01:00:24,287 --> 01:00:26,748
And now, I'm about to become a wife.

1374
01:00:27,624 --> 01:00:29,543
<i>So to be honest with you,</i>

1375
01:00:29,626 --> 01:00:31,628
I don't even know who I really am anymore.

1376
01:00:33,004 --> 01:00:34,422
What about you?

1377
01:00:34,506 --> 01:00:36,174
If you were the candidate,

1378
01:00:36,258 --> 01:00:37,300
how would you do it?

1379
01:00:38,385 --> 01:00:40,011
I'm not the candidate. You are.

1380
01:00:40,095 --> 01:00:41,138
I know.

1381
01:00:41,221 --> 01:00:43,557
But I need to understand
what you're looking for.

1382
01:00:44,182 --> 01:00:46,268
So, show me?

1383
01:00:54,901 --> 01:00:59,531
[gentle music playing]

1384
01:01:26,433 --> 01:01:29,311
[Angelo cooing softly]

1385
01:01:48,538 --> 01:01:53,960
[gentle music continues]

1386
01:02:01,009 --> 01:02:02,719
What do you call that walk?

1387
01:02:05,138 --> 01:02:06,640
That's the Mama walk.

1388
01:02:08,558 --> 01:02:10,727
Can that be my signature walk?

1389
01:02:13,021 --> 01:02:15,381
[Twinkle] <i>Mother, I can't shake</i>
<i>off these negative feelings.</i>

1390
01:02:16,149 --> 01:02:17,859
I want to be more open toward Mara,

1391
01:02:17,943 --> 01:02:20,278
but whenever she shows interest in Angelo,

1392
01:02:20,362 --> 01:02:22,322
and I see them getting close,

1393
01:02:22,405 --> 01:02:23,823
I get annoyed.

1394
01:02:23,907 --> 01:02:24,950
Is that wrong?

1395
01:02:25,033 --> 01:02:26,576
It's normal.

1396
01:02:26,660 --> 01:02:28,662
It's natural to feel threatened by Mara

1397
01:02:28,745 --> 01:02:31,790
since she's Angelo's biological mother.

1398
01:02:31,873 --> 01:02:34,668
But now, she's signed the adoption papers.

1399
01:02:34,751 --> 01:02:37,087
So don't worry about it anymore.

1400
01:02:37,170 --> 01:02:39,172
I don't know. I have a bad feeling.

1401
01:02:46,263 --> 01:02:47,343
[Mama M] What's the matter?

1402
01:02:49,057 --> 01:02:50,433
- Mister?
- Yes?

1403
01:02:50,517 --> 01:02:52,310
Where's the red bike?

1404
01:02:52,394 --> 01:02:54,521
It's gone. I already sold it.

1405
01:02:54,604 --> 01:02:58,316
Why did you sell it?
My son looks at it every day.

1406
01:02:58,400 --> 01:03:01,653
He was expecting it as his birthday gift.
Didn't I tell you to reserve it?

1407
01:03:01,736 --> 01:03:03,822
You've been reserving it for six months.

1408
01:03:03,905 --> 01:03:06,157
But no down payment.

1409
01:03:06,741 --> 01:03:08,576
Someone came here to buy it,

1410
01:03:08,660 --> 01:03:10,287
so I sold it to them.

1411
01:03:10,370 --> 01:03:11,955
My goodness.

1412
01:03:12,038 --> 01:03:17,085
- What now? The bike's gone!
- It's fine, we'll just look elsewhere.

1413
01:03:17,168 --> 01:03:18,769
No, the price is double everywhere else.

1414
01:03:18,837 --> 01:03:21,715
And that red bike,
Angelo really wanted that one.

1415
01:03:22,340 --> 01:03:24,759
I can't believe this guy!

1416
01:03:26,636 --> 01:03:29,347
[singing] <i>♪ Happy birthday to you! ♪</i>

1417
01:03:29,431 --> 01:03:31,266
<i>- ♪ Happy birthday ♪
- ♪ Happy birthday ♪</i>

1418
01:03:31,349 --> 01:03:34,519
- <i>♪ Happy birthda</i>... <i> ♪</i>
- <i>♪ Happy birthday ♪</i>

1419
01:03:34,602 --> 01:03:36,938
<i>♪ Happy birthday to you ♪</i>

1420
01:03:37,022 --> 01:03:43,695
<i>♪ Happy birthday to-o-o ♪</i>

1421
01:03:43,778 --> 01:03:45,780
<i>♪ You, baby! ♪</i>

1422
01:03:45,864 --> 01:03:48,742
[chuckles]

1423
01:03:48,825 --> 01:03:50,535
Happy birthday, my son!

1424
01:03:50,618 --> 01:03:52,120
[cheering and clapping]

1425
01:03:52,203 --> 01:03:54,914
Blow! Blow out the candle.

1426
01:03:54,998 --> 01:03:57,584
- [blows]
- [cheering and clapping]

1427
01:03:57,667 --> 01:03:59,586
Can we open the gifts now?

1428
01:04:01,504 --> 01:04:02,922
Uh, yeah! Sure, go ahead, son.

1429
01:04:03,006 --> 01:04:04,132
[Vince] Yes, gifts!

1430
01:04:04,215 --> 01:04:05,759
- Okay.
- That one.

1431
01:04:06,384 --> 01:04:08,553
Let's do the big one!

1432
01:04:08,636 --> 01:04:10,263
It's Mother's big surprise!

1433
01:04:10,347 --> 01:04:12,074
- Shall we open it, Angelo?
- It's huge, right?

1434
01:04:12,098 --> 01:04:13,200
Okay, let's do it together...

1435
01:04:13,224 --> 01:04:16,644
In three, two, one!

1436
01:04:16,728 --> 01:04:18,313
Hey!

1437
01:04:20,607 --> 01:04:22,192
[boy] Just a helmet?

1438
01:04:24,527 --> 01:04:26,321
Where's the bike?

1439
01:04:28,406 --> 01:04:29,741
Isn't it nice?

1440
01:04:29,824 --> 01:04:30,824
Helmet?

1441
01:04:33,453 --> 01:04:35,622
Yup, sweetie. This is what's trending now.

1442
01:04:35,705 --> 01:04:38,333
You wear the helmet,
and the bike goes on your head.

1443
01:04:38,416 --> 01:04:40,293
[awkward chuckle]

1444
01:04:45,590 --> 01:04:47,342
Sorry, sweetie.

1445
01:04:47,425 --> 01:04:48,885
Helmet first, okay?

1446
01:04:48,968 --> 01:04:50,345
My baby…

1447
01:04:50,428 --> 01:04:52,347
But I'll get it for you later.

1448
01:04:52,430 --> 01:04:53,556
[boys laughing]

1449
01:04:53,640 --> 01:04:55,975
- Hey!
- He got a stupid helmet!

1450
01:04:56,059 --> 01:04:57,059
[Twinkle] Hey, hey, hey!

1451
01:04:57,102 --> 01:04:58,186
[sobbing]

1452
01:04:58,269 --> 01:04:59,646
Son…

1453
01:04:59,729 --> 01:05:01,940
It's really nice, though.

1454
01:05:02,023 --> 01:05:03,566
Don't cry.

1455
01:05:04,192 --> 01:05:05,193
Try it on.

1456
01:05:05,276 --> 01:05:07,821
This helmet's important too.

1457
01:05:07,904 --> 01:05:09,239
Son…

1458
01:05:10,573 --> 01:05:12,033
[bicycle bell rings]

1459
01:05:13,993 --> 01:05:15,078
[bicycle bell rings]

1460
01:05:16,830 --> 01:05:21,334
[whimsical music playing]

1461
01:05:28,800 --> 01:05:30,601
[Mara] I see you
post about this all the time.

1462
01:05:30,635 --> 01:05:33,638
So I thought maybe this is
what you'd want for your birthday.

1463
01:05:34,264 --> 01:05:35,890
This is my dream bike!

1464
01:05:35,974 --> 01:05:40,979
[clapping]

1465
01:05:41,062 --> 01:05:42,605
[softly] I thought we had a deal.

1466
01:05:43,690 --> 01:05:45,316
How dare you do this to me?

1467
01:05:46,234 --> 01:05:47,444
Get out.

1468
01:05:49,362 --> 01:05:50,655
[Twinkle] Get out of my house!

1469
01:05:50,738 --> 01:05:52,323
Carry your bike with you.

1470
01:05:52,991 --> 01:05:54,200
Get out of my house!

1471
01:05:54,284 --> 01:05:55,577
Get out!

1472
01:05:55,660 --> 01:05:57,036
[bicycle bell rings]

1473
01:05:59,873 --> 01:06:04,586
[screaming]

1474
01:06:05,753 --> 01:06:07,922
- [Angelo] Ma!
- [screaming stops]

1475
01:06:08,006 --> 01:06:09,340
Yes, what is this?

1476
01:06:09,424 --> 01:06:10,550
[screaming]

1477
01:06:10,633 --> 01:06:11,759
What a cool bike!

1478
01:06:11,843 --> 01:06:13,678
And it's red!
Perfect for you, sweetie!

1479
01:06:13,761 --> 01:06:15,513
Right? Say yes!

1480
01:06:15,597 --> 01:06:16,473
It's amazing!

1481
01:06:16,556 --> 01:06:20,477
[awkward chuckle]

1482
01:06:22,395 --> 01:06:24,439
Sorry again, son, okay?

1483
01:06:25,398 --> 01:06:27,484
But happy birthday anyway.

1484
01:06:27,567 --> 01:06:29,360
I love you so much, Mama!

1485
01:06:30,403 --> 01:06:31,403
You are so sweet.

1486
01:06:31,446 --> 01:06:33,215
- Say it again, please...
- Happy birthday, Angelo!

1487
01:06:33,239 --> 01:06:34,991
Thank you, Miss Mara.

1488
01:06:35,074 --> 01:06:36,910
You saved my birthday.

1489
01:06:36,993 --> 01:06:38,745
- Aww.
- Aww.

1490
01:06:38,828 --> 01:06:40,246
Welcome!

1491
01:06:41,915 --> 01:06:43,041
[boy] Come on, Angelo!

1492
01:06:43,124 --> 01:06:45,084
Let's try your new bike.

1493
01:06:45,168 --> 01:06:47,545
[Mama M laughs] Don't go
on the street, okay?

1494
01:06:47,629 --> 01:06:49,148
- [Mara] Be careful!
- [Mama M] Stay in the yard!

1495
01:06:49,172 --> 01:06:50,798
Angelo, the hel...

1496
01:06:50,882 --> 01:06:53,468
Son, put on the helmet!

1497
01:06:53,551 --> 01:06:56,137
- [Mama M] Oh, the food!
- [Mayet] Oh yeah.

1498
01:06:56,221 --> 01:06:58,473
Son, the helmet!

1499
01:06:58,556 --> 01:07:01,851
[indistinct chatter]

1500
01:07:06,606 --> 01:07:07,857
[washing dishes]

1501
01:07:07,941 --> 01:07:09,400
Let me help you with that.

1502
01:07:14,531 --> 01:07:15,990
I'm thinking,

1503
01:07:16,074 --> 01:07:19,494
what if next year, for Angelo's birthday,

1504
01:07:19,577 --> 01:07:21,329
we go to Japan?

1505
01:07:21,412 --> 01:07:23,331
Or maybe Paris?

1506
01:07:23,414 --> 01:07:25,542
What other countries do you want to visit?

1507
01:07:25,625 --> 01:07:26,709
Nah, it's okay.

1508
01:07:26,793 --> 01:07:27,961
Too expensive.

1509
01:07:28,044 --> 01:07:30,547
And we're leaving soon, right?
We're moving to Hong Kong.

1510
01:07:30,630 --> 01:07:33,007
Ah, right. I'll visit you there.

1511
01:07:34,884 --> 01:07:37,053
Tomorrow, you're locked in
for Miss Uniworld.

1512
01:07:37,136 --> 01:07:38,763
And the petition will start moving.

1513
01:07:42,058 --> 01:07:44,143
I'm aware of that. And?

1514
01:07:44,227 --> 01:07:45,270
We're done.

1515
01:07:47,897 --> 01:07:49,983
Twinkle, is this about the bike?

1516
01:07:51,317 --> 01:07:54,737
I honestly didn't know
you were planning to buy that for Angelo.

1517
01:07:57,699 --> 01:07:58,992
Your training is over.

1518
01:07:59,576 --> 01:08:01,995
So there's no reason for us
to see each other anymore.

1519
01:08:02,078 --> 01:08:05,290
And don't show up for Angelo either.
Do you understand?

1520
01:08:07,542 --> 01:08:09,711
What if I still want to get to know him?

1521
01:08:11,087 --> 01:08:13,965
You can't deny the fact that
I'm still part of his life.

1522
01:08:14,048 --> 01:08:15,967
I've grown to love that child too.

1523
01:08:16,050 --> 01:08:19,012
If you really love that child,
leave us alone.

1524
01:08:19,095 --> 01:08:22,765
You'll only make things harder for Angelo
when we leave if you keep sticking around.

1525
01:08:24,809 --> 01:08:26,060
Think about him for once.

1526
01:08:34,902 --> 01:08:37,405
[water running]

1527
01:08:37,488 --> 01:08:40,575
[footsteps retreating]

1528
01:08:52,337 --> 01:08:53,755
Miss Mara!

1529
01:08:54,797 --> 01:08:56,466
Are you leaving already?

1530
01:08:57,050 --> 01:08:58,176
Yeah.

1531
01:08:58,760 --> 01:09:00,887
Happy birthday again, Angelo.

1532
01:09:01,429 --> 01:09:03,640
I just want to give you something.

1533
01:09:10,605 --> 01:09:12,982
Thank you. It's beautiful.

1534
01:09:13,775 --> 01:09:16,235
Where are you really going?

1535
01:09:18,696 --> 01:09:21,407
Miss Uniworld will start soon.

1536
01:09:21,491 --> 01:09:24,327
Mama trained you, right?

1537
01:09:25,203 --> 01:09:28,247
I'm sure you're going to win.

1538
01:09:30,833 --> 01:09:32,794
Be a good boy, Angelo.

1539
01:09:33,586 --> 01:09:35,088
You're acting weird.

1540
01:09:35,171 --> 01:09:37,507
It feels like you're saying goodbye.

1541
01:09:38,883 --> 01:09:42,720
It's just going to take a while
before we see each other again.

1542
01:09:43,304 --> 01:09:44,430
That's too bad.

1543
01:09:44,514 --> 01:09:47,266
You won't get to see me
learn how to ride a bike.

1544
01:09:48,101 --> 01:09:53,523
[soft music playing]

1545
01:10:00,697 --> 01:10:02,573
Can you wait for me?

1546
01:10:02,657 --> 01:10:04,537
I'll be the one to teach you
how to ride a bike.

1547
01:10:04,575 --> 01:10:06,202
Sure!

1548
01:10:06,869 --> 01:10:08,663
And after Miss Uniworld,

1549
01:10:08,746 --> 01:10:10,748
I'll teach you how to skate,

1550
01:10:10,832 --> 01:10:13,543
play soccer, swim...

1551
01:10:13,626 --> 01:10:16,504
Anything you want to learn,
I'll teach you.

1552
01:10:16,587 --> 01:10:18,631
Wow, really?

1553
01:10:19,799 --> 01:10:22,009
Just wait for me, okay?

1554
01:10:22,593 --> 01:10:24,345
And when I come back,

1555
01:10:24,429 --> 01:10:25,847
I won't ever leave again.

1556
01:10:25,930 --> 01:10:26,930
Promise.

1557
01:10:26,973 --> 01:10:28,266
Promise?

1558
01:10:29,183 --> 01:10:30,476
[sniffles]

1559
01:10:31,018 --> 01:10:32,270
[Mara] Promise.

1560
01:10:33,438 --> 01:10:36,065
[sobs, sniffles]

1561
01:10:51,456 --> 01:10:54,959
[pageant music beating]

1562
01:11:03,968 --> 01:11:07,388
- [Angelo] Miss Mara!
- [cheering]

1563
01:11:07,472 --> 01:11:10,266
- Her gown is stunning!
- Go, Miss Mara!

1564
01:11:10,349 --> 01:11:11,809
- [cheering]
- [Angelo] Go, Miss Mara!

1565
01:11:11,893 --> 01:11:14,479
- [pageant host] <i>Live at the Big Dome.</i>
- [Angelo] Miss Mara!

1566
01:11:14,562 --> 01:11:20,067
<i>- This is Miss Uniworld Philippines 2025!</i>
- [Angelo] Miss Mara!

1567
01:11:20,151 --> 01:11:22,445
- Finally!
- [cheering]

1568
01:11:25,656 --> 01:11:32,163
[upbeat music playing]

1569
01:11:38,002 --> 01:11:41,088
Miss Mara!

1570
01:11:41,923 --> 01:11:48,679
[upbeat music continues]

1571
01:12:07,782 --> 01:12:08,699
[cheering]

1572
01:12:08,783 --> 01:12:10,660
You're so beautiful, Miss Mara!

1573
01:12:15,289 --> 01:12:21,921
[upbeat music continues]

1574
01:12:29,679 --> 01:12:31,389
[Angelo] Miss Mara!

1575
01:12:31,472 --> 01:12:35,434
[cheering]

1576
01:12:39,522 --> 01:12:41,107
Ma, why did you do that?

1577
01:12:41,190 --> 01:12:42,817
We're watching!

1578
01:12:42,900 --> 01:12:44,318
TV is bad for your body!

1579
01:12:44,402 --> 01:12:46,737
It'll weaken your lungs,
and you'll cough up blood.

1580
01:12:46,821 --> 01:12:47,655
- [gasping]
- TB?

1581
01:12:47,738 --> 01:12:49,782
Mother, that's a different thing.

1582
01:12:49,866 --> 01:12:51,075
It's still TB.

1583
01:12:51,909 --> 01:12:53,202
Neri, take this out.

1584
01:12:53,286 --> 01:12:54,745
Put it in storage.

1585
01:12:54,829 --> 01:12:58,082
- Seriously, Mother?
- How are we supposed to watch the pageant?

1586
01:12:58,165 --> 01:13:00,585
[Vince] Mother, come on, no to censorship!

1587
01:13:00,668 --> 01:13:02,753
- Yeah.
- We'll just watch on our phones, then.

1588
01:13:02,837 --> 01:13:04,213
- Come on.
- Your phone.

1589
01:13:04,297 --> 01:13:05,590
Why won't it connect?

1590
01:13:05,673 --> 01:13:08,843
No Wi-Fi either.
I cut it off to save money.

1591
01:13:08,926 --> 01:13:10,386
- Mother!
- This is ridiculous.

1592
01:13:10,469 --> 01:13:11,971
Why didn't you follow Ria's example?

1593
01:13:12,054 --> 01:13:13,639
She boycotted Miss Uniworld.

1594
01:13:13,723 --> 01:13:15,641
She boycotted because she had a date.

1595
01:13:15,725 --> 01:13:17,452
Mother, the whole Philippines
is waiting to see

1596
01:13:17,476 --> 01:13:19,645
if Miss Mara will finally win the crown.

1597
01:13:19,729 --> 01:13:22,690
- That's right!
- Mother, we can't miss this!

1598
01:13:22,773 --> 01:13:24,775
No watching, end of story!

1599
01:13:24,859 --> 01:13:28,613
Our snacks are here for our viewing party!

1600
01:13:28,696 --> 01:13:29,822
Oh!

1601
01:13:29,906 --> 01:13:31,198
Where'd the TV go?

1602
01:13:31,282 --> 01:13:32,992
Ma, I have to watch!

1603
01:13:33,075 --> 01:13:34,994
I want to cheer for Miss Mara!

1604
01:13:35,077 --> 01:13:36,162
[Twinkle] Angelo!

1605
01:13:36,245 --> 01:13:37,496
Where are you...?
Angelo!

1606
01:13:37,580 --> 01:13:39,665
Get back here. Where are you going?

1607
01:13:39,749 --> 01:13:44,337
[soft music playing]

1608
01:14:15,368 --> 01:14:17,703
[Angelo] Go, Guardian Angel Miss Mara!

1609
01:14:22,208 --> 01:14:24,752
- [Angelo exhales excitedly]
- [vendor] Oh!

1610
01:14:25,378 --> 01:14:30,424
["Tala" instrumental playing]

1611
01:15:01,080 --> 01:15:02,498
[vendor] There she is. Wow!

1612
01:15:04,166 --> 01:15:05,459
- Angelo!
- Wow!

1613
01:15:05,543 --> 01:15:07,503
I've been looking for you.
You've been right here.

1614
01:15:07,545 --> 01:15:08,713
What are you doing here?

1615
01:15:09,755 --> 01:15:11,173
Watching!

1616
01:15:11,757 --> 01:15:13,217
Come on, let's go home!

1617
01:15:14,427 --> 01:15:15,594
Come...

1618
01:15:15,678 --> 01:15:17,013
[people scream]

1619
01:15:17,096 --> 01:15:19,515
Come on! Angelo,
I'm going to get mad at you!

1620
01:15:19,598 --> 01:15:22,893
[people scream and cheer]

1621
01:15:22,977 --> 01:15:23,977
Ange...

1622
01:15:24,979 --> 01:15:26,689
- You're making me angry!
- [people scream]

1623
01:15:26,772 --> 01:15:27,690
I'm watching!

1624
01:15:27,773 --> 01:15:30,026
You can't. I told you
not to watch that show!

1625
01:15:30,109 --> 01:15:31,861
Angelo, I need you to stop right now.

1626
01:15:31,944 --> 01:15:37,074
[people cheering]

1627
01:15:37,158 --> 01:15:38,576
I'm getting angry!

1628
01:15:38,659 --> 01:15:40,369
- No! Come...
- I'm watching!

1629
01:15:40,453 --> 01:15:41,787
Let's go home!

1630
01:15:42,455 --> 01:15:44,999
[host] <i>The first queen to secure her spot</i>

1631
01:15:45,082 --> 01:15:47,626
<i>in the final three is…</i>

1632
01:15:48,169 --> 01:15:49,754
<i>Miss Albay!</i>

1633
01:15:49,837 --> 01:15:51,672
[cheering]

1634
01:15:51,756 --> 01:15:56,218
- Oh my!
- This is it!

1635
01:15:56,302 --> 01:15:58,054
Didn't I say no one should watch?

1636
01:16:00,639 --> 01:16:01,891
That's enough!

1637
01:16:01,974 --> 01:16:03,768
What are you afraid of?

1638
01:16:03,851 --> 01:16:06,395
Isn't the petition about to start?

1639
01:16:06,479 --> 01:16:11,859
And don't you want to see the result
of all your hard work? Sit down!

1640
01:16:11,942 --> 01:16:14,987
[host] <i>Our second queen to make this cut</i>

1641
01:16:15,071 --> 01:16:16,405
<i>representing…</i>

1642
01:16:17,323 --> 01:16:20,034
[cheering]

1643
01:16:20,618 --> 01:16:23,370
<i>Representing the city of love,</i>

1644
01:16:23,454 --> 01:16:25,581
<i>it's Miss Iloilo!</i>

1645
01:16:25,664 --> 01:16:27,666
[screams] I swear I'll protest

1646
01:16:27,750 --> 01:16:30,586
if Miss Mara doesn't make it
to the top three!

1647
01:16:30,669 --> 01:16:31,587
[excited chatter]

1648
01:16:31,670 --> 01:16:34,799
<i>And now, for the final coveted spot,</i>

1649
01:16:34,882 --> 01:16:38,344
<i>the last queen to make it
to our top three…</i>

1650
01:16:39,929 --> 01:16:41,430
[excited murmuring]

1651
01:16:44,100 --> 01:16:46,894
<i>From a city that has been synonymous</i>

1652
01:16:46,977 --> 01:16:50,022
<i>with a new era of public service…</i>

1653
01:16:50,106 --> 01:16:51,899
[deafening cheers on TV]

1654
01:16:51,982 --> 01:16:55,027
<i>…the last queen standing is…</i>

1655
01:16:55,111 --> 01:16:57,446
[cheering on TV continues]

1656
01:17:00,032 --> 01:17:02,493
<i>…Miss Pasig!</i>

1657
01:17:02,576 --> 01:17:08,707
- [cheering]
- ["Tala" by Bryan Chong playing]

1658
01:17:13,796 --> 01:17:15,965
Miss Mara!

1659
01:17:16,048 --> 01:17:20,094
- [cheering continues]
- ["Tala" continues]

1660
01:17:20,177 --> 01:17:21,804
Mara!

1661
01:17:21,887 --> 01:17:23,848
[woman] Go, Mara!

1662
01:17:23,931 --> 01:17:25,700
- [host] <i>Ladies and gentlemen!</i>
- Here she comes!

1663
01:17:25,724 --> 01:17:29,270
<i>Let's give a big round of applause
to your official Final 3.</i>

1664
01:17:29,353 --> 01:17:31,856
<i>They are just one step away
from the crown.</i>

1665
01:17:31,939 --> 01:17:33,023
Oh my God!

1666
01:17:33,107 --> 01:17:36,527
You will really be the problem
if she faints again!

1667
01:17:37,611 --> 01:17:40,447
All right, Miss Pasig.

1668
01:17:40,531 --> 01:17:42,449
Please come forward.

1669
01:17:43,284 --> 01:17:45,536
[cheering]

1670
01:17:45,619 --> 01:17:46,954
Let's go, Mara!

1671
01:17:48,122 --> 01:17:49,582
Good evening, Miss Pasig.

1672
01:17:49,665 --> 01:17:51,750
Are you ready for your question?

1673
01:17:51,834 --> 01:17:52,835
Yes.

1674
01:17:52,918 --> 01:17:55,129
All right, here we go.

1675
01:17:55,921 --> 01:17:59,550
What do you think is the biggest problem

1676
01:17:59,633 --> 01:18:02,178
young people are facing today?

1677
01:18:07,349 --> 01:18:10,102
Would you like me to repeat
the question, Miss Pasig?

1678
01:18:10,186 --> 01:18:11,604
<i>No.</i>

1679
01:18:12,271 --> 01:18:16,817
<i>I'd like to take this moment
to answer a question from ten years ago.</i>

1680
01:18:18,110 --> 01:18:20,946
[host] <i>Miss Pasig, I'm not sure</i>
<i>you're allowed to do that.</i>

1681
01:18:21,030 --> 01:18:22,281
<i>Is it okay?</i>

1682
01:18:24,742 --> 01:18:26,035
All right, Miss Pasig.

1683
01:18:26,702 --> 01:18:27,702
Thank you.

1684
01:18:28,662 --> 01:18:30,206
[Mara] The question was,

1685
01:18:30,289 --> 01:18:32,791
if I were to become a mother,

1686
01:18:33,751 --> 01:18:37,087
would I prioritize
my dreams over my child?

1687
01:18:38,839 --> 01:18:40,466
<i>My answer then,</i>

1688
01:18:41,467 --> 01:18:43,177
<i>and my truth is…</i>

1689
01:18:45,679 --> 01:18:46,680
<i>Yes.</i>

1690
01:18:48,224 --> 01:18:49,224
[Mara] <i>I would.</i>

1691
01:18:51,477 --> 01:18:52,478
Because...

1692
01:18:53,145 --> 01:18:54,688
Because I wasn't ready.

1693
01:18:57,399 --> 01:18:59,777
Because I wasn't fit to be a mother.

1694
01:19:03,405 --> 01:19:07,201
I was 18, and I had big dreams.

1695
01:19:10,120 --> 01:19:12,539
<i>They say that the person
that's hardest to forgive</i>

1696
01:19:12,623 --> 01:19:14,416
<i>is the version of yourself</i>

1697
01:19:16,085 --> 01:19:17,670
<i>that didn't know better.</i>

1698
01:19:20,256 --> 01:19:22,383
To my family,

1699
01:19:24,218 --> 01:19:25,970
and to Anton…

1700
01:19:30,307 --> 01:19:33,227
And to everyone who has stood by me,

1701
01:19:34,520 --> 01:19:37,398
you deserve the truth from me.

1702
01:19:44,363 --> 01:19:45,990
Ten years ago,

1703
01:19:47,074 --> 01:19:49,910
I gave birth to a beautiful baby boy.

1704
01:19:53,080 --> 01:19:56,000
And his name is Angelo.

1705
01:19:57,710 --> 01:19:59,128
[Mara] <i>I...</i>

1706
01:19:59,211 --> 01:20:00,629
<i>I abandoned him.</i>

1707
01:20:04,800 --> 01:20:08,512
<i>I gave him to the best mother
that he could ever have.</i>

1708
01:20:09,430 --> 01:20:10,597
<i>My coach,</i>

1709
01:20:12,057 --> 01:20:13,057
<i>Twinkle.</i>

1710
01:20:14,893 --> 01:20:17,604
<i>Who I'm very, very grateful for.</i>

1711
01:20:17,688 --> 01:20:19,273
[sobbing]

1712
01:20:23,694 --> 01:20:25,279
Shut that thing off.
Where's the remote?

1713
01:20:34,705 --> 01:20:36,332
Is she my real mom?

1714
01:20:36,415 --> 01:20:40,210
[sobbing continues]

1715
01:20:56,185 --> 01:20:57,311
That's right.

1716
01:20:58,937 --> 01:21:00,397
She's your mother.

1717
01:21:01,357 --> 01:21:05,152
Why didn't you tell me that
she was my mother?

1718
01:21:08,530 --> 01:21:11,533
Wait, let me explain.

1719
01:21:11,617 --> 01:21:15,621
[both sobbing]

1720
01:21:21,835 --> 01:21:25,839
- [Mama M shushes]
- [sobbing continues]

1721
01:21:31,178 --> 01:21:32,971
For so many years,

1722
01:21:34,306 --> 01:21:37,226
I really wish I could've
done things differently.

1723
01:21:41,980 --> 01:21:43,315
[Mara] <i>But now…</i>

1724
01:21:45,526 --> 01:21:48,904
<i>I'm finally ready to accept my truth.</i>

1725
01:21:54,076 --> 01:21:55,577
I'm a mother.

1726
01:21:57,538 --> 01:22:00,374
And I'm proud to share that to everyone.

1727
01:22:05,087 --> 01:22:05,921
Come on!

1728
01:22:06,004 --> 01:22:07,548
- Ma?
- No!

1729
01:22:07,631 --> 01:22:08,924
[Nanette] Let's go!

1730
01:22:21,770 --> 01:22:25,023
[audience cheering, clapping]

1731
01:22:25,107 --> 01:22:27,526
We love you, Mara!

1732
01:22:29,027 --> 01:22:31,155
Go, Mara!

1733
01:22:35,909 --> 01:22:42,249
[soft music playing]

1734
01:23:13,655 --> 01:23:14,781
Sweetie…

1735
01:23:16,617 --> 01:23:18,076
I'm really sorry.

1736
01:23:28,462 --> 01:23:31,089
Is that why she came here?

1737
01:23:31,590 --> 01:23:34,051
Is that why she bought me the bike?

1738
01:23:34,134 --> 01:23:36,386
Because she's my real mom?

1739
01:23:41,934 --> 01:23:44,269
Are you mad at her?

1740
01:23:44,353 --> 01:23:47,856
Is that why you didn't want
to tell me she's my real mom?

1741
01:23:53,862 --> 01:23:56,240
I just don't want to lose you.

1742
01:23:58,116 --> 01:24:00,744
Why would you lose me, Ma?

1743
01:24:06,250 --> 01:24:08,210
I'm so scared.

1744
01:24:09,461 --> 01:24:12,839
I got scared thinking what might happen.

1745
01:24:16,593 --> 01:24:17,803
Sweetie,

1746
01:24:19,596 --> 01:24:21,181
are you mad at me?

1747
01:24:22,266 --> 01:24:28,146
I'm still a little annoyed
because you lied to me.

1748
01:24:28,230 --> 01:24:31,525
[soft music playing]

1749
01:24:34,319 --> 01:24:35,737
Do you

1750
01:24:36,697 --> 01:24:39,658
want Mayet to stay with you tonight
instead of me?

1751
01:24:40,409 --> 01:24:44,413
I can't sleep if you're not beside me.

1752
01:24:52,337 --> 01:24:54,923
I will never leave your side.

1753
01:24:56,758 --> 01:24:58,176
That's my promise.

1754
01:25:12,649 --> 01:25:14,568
[sobbing]

1755
01:25:38,175 --> 01:25:44,681
[soft music continues]

1756
01:25:54,191 --> 01:25:57,986
This is the written consent
that we talked about.

1757
01:25:58,737 --> 01:26:02,866
You do understand that
your Mama Twinkle is adopting you,

1758
01:26:02,949 --> 01:26:03,949
don't you?

1759
01:26:05,952 --> 01:26:09,706
Okay, so, here.

1760
01:26:10,415 --> 01:26:16,380
On this paper,
just write everything you feel.

1761
01:26:17,589 --> 01:26:21,426
Whether you agree or not.

1762
01:26:22,302 --> 01:26:25,430
Whatever you want to say,
just put it there.

1763
01:26:28,517 --> 01:26:31,186
You love your Mama Twinkle, don't you?

1764
01:26:34,439 --> 01:26:35,899
Okay.

1765
01:26:39,736 --> 01:26:45,617
[soft music playing]

1766
01:26:59,297 --> 01:27:01,174
Does he really have to do this?

1767
01:27:02,592 --> 01:27:07,514
Since Angelo is now ten years old,
he has the right to choose.

1768
01:27:08,557 --> 01:27:11,935
[Mutya] It's important
that the consent comes from him

1769
01:27:12,728 --> 01:27:14,896
if he wants you to adopt him.

1770
01:27:14,980 --> 01:27:17,107
I AM ANGELO REYES. THE MOM I WANT IS…

1771
01:27:17,190 --> 01:27:19,109
[Angelo sobbing]

1772
01:27:26,575 --> 01:27:30,203
[sobbing continues]

1773
01:27:54,019 --> 01:27:55,729
Angelo, sweetie.

1774
01:27:57,606 --> 01:28:00,942
If this is hard for you,
you don't have to force yourself, okay?

1775
01:28:01,526 --> 01:28:04,112
We can wait a little longer, okay?

1776
01:28:09,326 --> 01:28:13,538
[soft music continues]

1777
01:28:15,081 --> 01:28:17,167
[cell phone chimes, buzzes]

1778
01:28:22,589 --> 01:28:23,965
[Mutya] Excuse me.

1779
01:28:30,806 --> 01:28:31,806
Um,

1780
01:28:32,974 --> 01:28:36,978
Mara filed a petition
to retract her signature.

1781
01:28:39,523 --> 01:28:40,816
So what happens now?

1782
01:28:41,525 --> 01:28:46,947
We'll review Mara's case again
and see if she can prove

1783
01:28:47,030 --> 01:28:50,242
that she's ready to be Angelo's mother.

1784
01:28:50,325 --> 01:28:51,827
What, she's taking him?

1785
01:28:51,910 --> 01:28:53,662
[Mutya] Not yet.

1786
01:28:54,287 --> 01:28:57,749
But we explained this
to you before, right?

1787
01:28:57,833 --> 01:29:01,795
That if the biological mother
changes her mind,

1788
01:29:01,878 --> 01:29:04,548
we will do everything possible
to reunite them.

1789
01:29:05,715 --> 01:29:07,175
No. Get out. Leave.

1790
01:29:07,676 --> 01:29:08,510
Leave.

1791
01:29:08,593 --> 01:29:09,970
- Twinkle.
- Ma!

1792
01:29:10,053 --> 01:29:11,596
Calm down.

1793
01:29:13,265 --> 01:29:14,474
Calm down?

1794
01:29:14,975 --> 01:29:17,644
You're taking my child from me,
and you want me to calm down?

1795
01:29:17,727 --> 01:29:19,771
She can't take Angelo from me.

1796
01:29:19,855 --> 01:29:23,108
Mara can't take my son.
I'll take him far away.

1797
01:29:23,191 --> 01:29:24,860
You can't do that.

1798
01:29:25,443 --> 01:29:26,903
You can be charged with kidnapping.

1799
01:29:26,987 --> 01:29:29,656
Kidnapping? I'm his mother. He's my child.

1800
01:29:29,739 --> 01:29:31,658
Do you hear what you're saying?

1801
01:29:31,741 --> 01:29:33,243
You can't take my child!

1802
01:29:33,326 --> 01:29:34,828
Please leave.

1803
01:29:35,370 --> 01:29:36,788
Leave!

1804
01:29:53,096 --> 01:29:54,365
[Vince] Hey, it's a long weekend.

1805
01:29:54,389 --> 01:29:57,517
Everyone in the house went out of town.
When will it be our turn?

1806
01:29:57,601 --> 01:29:59,269
I have an idea. Let's go to the beach.

1807
01:29:59,352 --> 01:30:00,352
I'm in!

1808
01:30:00,395 --> 01:30:02,522
[Angelo] Ma, where are we going?

1809
01:30:02,606 --> 01:30:04,316
Twinkle, you know this is wrong.

1810
01:30:04,399 --> 01:30:05,859
Don't let your emotions take over.

1811
01:30:05,942 --> 01:30:07,753
Let's all have dinner first,
so you can calm down?

1812
01:30:07,777 --> 01:30:09,578
Yes. I cooked dinner for us.
Come back inside!

1813
01:30:09,654 --> 01:30:12,574
- Come back upstairs.
- Let's talk things over.

1814
01:30:12,657 --> 01:30:14,385
- Come on, Twinkle.
- Mother, where are you going?

1815
01:30:14,409 --> 01:30:15,577
Hail me a taxi, please.

1816
01:30:15,660 --> 01:30:17,287
Twinkle.

1817
01:30:21,666 --> 01:30:22,792
What is this?

1818
01:30:23,585 --> 01:30:25,128
Why did you bring guards with you?

1819
01:30:25,211 --> 01:30:27,505
You threatened to run away with Angelo.

1820
01:30:27,589 --> 01:30:30,425
I can't allow that to happen, Twinkle.

1821
01:30:31,134 --> 01:30:33,534
You really think I'll hand my son
over to you just like that?

1822
01:30:34,054 --> 01:30:35,221
[Mutya] I'm sorry.

1823
01:30:35,305 --> 01:30:39,476
We wouldn't be here if you'd stayed calm.

1824
01:30:40,310 --> 01:30:43,855
Now, we need to place him
in a temporary home.

1825
01:30:44,481 --> 01:30:46,650
You can't take my son away from me.

1826
01:30:47,275 --> 01:30:49,694
Twinkle, calm down.

1827
01:30:50,445 --> 01:30:51,863
You're scaring the child.

1828
01:30:51,946 --> 01:30:54,824
Calm down? With what you're doing?!
With all these guards with you?!

1829
01:30:54,908 --> 01:30:58,536
Everything we're doing
is for Angelo's safety.

1830
01:30:58,620 --> 01:31:03,667
We want to make sure he's okay
while we review the petition.

1831
01:31:03,750 --> 01:31:05,585
Are you implying
he wouldn't be safe with me?

1832
01:31:05,669 --> 01:31:06,503
Huh?

1833
01:31:06,586 --> 01:31:08,546
You are messing with our lives.

1834
01:31:09,130 --> 01:31:10,840
I'll never part with my child.

1835
01:31:10,924 --> 01:31:12,217
Leave us alone.

1836
01:31:12,300 --> 01:31:14,180
- Come on, Angelo.
- [man] We're taking the child.

1837
01:31:14,219 --> 01:31:16,262
- Let's talk about this.
- [Twinkle] Leave us alone!

1838
01:31:16,346 --> 01:31:19,599
- Let's talk about this.
- [Twinkle] Back off!

1839
01:31:19,683 --> 01:31:23,061
- Let go!
- Stay out of this!

1840
01:31:23,144 --> 01:31:24,688
You are making a big mistake!

1841
01:31:24,771 --> 01:31:27,315
Angelo is Twinkle's son!

1842
01:31:27,399 --> 01:31:28,399
Leave them alone!

1843
01:31:28,441 --> 01:31:29,984
[man] Go after them! Go!

1844
01:31:30,068 --> 01:31:31,653
[Bea] That's our house!

1845
01:31:31,736 --> 01:31:32,904
[Marco] You leave!

1846
01:31:33,488 --> 01:31:37,242
- Ma! Don't give me to them!
- [door slams shut]

1847
01:31:37,325 --> 01:31:39,119
- [Angelo crying]
- No.

1848
01:31:39,202 --> 01:31:41,830
No, sweetie. You're staying with me.

1849
01:31:43,331 --> 01:31:44,374
[Mama M] Twinkle?

1850
01:31:44,457 --> 01:31:46,334
Twinkle, open the door!

1851
01:31:46,418 --> 01:31:48,670
You might regret this.

1852
01:31:48,753 --> 01:31:49,838
- Open the door!
- [knocking]

1853
01:31:49,921 --> 01:31:51,214
- Twinkle?
- [man] Open the door!

1854
01:31:51,297 --> 01:31:56,594
- [doorknob rattling]
- [Angelo continues crying]

1855
01:31:56,678 --> 01:31:57,971
[Mama M] Open up!

1856
01:31:58,054 --> 01:31:59,764
- Go away!
- [Mama M] Twinkle, open the door!

1857
01:31:59,848 --> 01:32:00,932
No one comes in!

1858
01:32:01,015 --> 01:32:02,600
Go away!

1859
01:32:02,684 --> 01:32:06,563
- Open the door! For God's sake.
- Go away! No one comes in!

1860
01:32:06,646 --> 01:32:09,983
- For God's sake.
- [Angelo keeps sobbing]

1861
01:32:10,567 --> 01:32:13,903
- [Mama M] You're scaring the kid.
- [man] Please open the door.

1862
01:32:13,987 --> 01:32:15,655
[man] Please open the door.

1863
01:32:15,739 --> 01:32:17,240
[Mama M] I'll handle this.

1864
01:32:17,323 --> 01:32:18,825
[Mama M] Let's all calm down.

1865
01:32:18,908 --> 01:32:20,326
Go away!

1866
01:32:20,410 --> 01:32:21,995
[Mama M] Please have pity on the child.

1867
01:32:22,078 --> 01:32:24,414
- [Mama M] Calm down, please.
- I will not give you to them.

1868
01:32:25,373 --> 01:32:26,734
- [glass shatters]
- [Angelo shrieks]

1869
01:32:26,791 --> 01:32:28,209
What is happening?!

1870
01:32:28,293 --> 01:32:29,335
- [door slams]
- [man] There.

1871
01:32:29,419 --> 01:32:31,880
- Go ahead, come closer!
- Twinkle, don't!

1872
01:32:31,963 --> 01:32:34,007
Come closer! I dare you!

1873
01:32:34,090 --> 01:32:35,967
- Ma!
- No one's taking my child.

1874
01:32:36,050 --> 01:32:37,594
You're scaring Angelo.

1875
01:32:37,677 --> 01:32:38,803
Ma!

1876
01:32:39,429 --> 01:32:41,765
- [Mutya] The kid is scared.
- [Angelo continues crying]

1877
01:32:44,684 --> 01:32:48,271
[breathing heavily]

1878
01:32:48,354 --> 01:32:49,189
[knife clatters]

1879
01:32:49,272 --> 01:32:51,441
- Get him!
- [Mama M] Be careful!

1880
01:32:51,524 --> 01:32:52,442
[Mama M] Goodness!

1881
01:32:52,525 --> 01:32:54,527
- [Mama M] Just a second!
- [Twinkle] Angelo!

1882
01:32:54,611 --> 01:32:56,172
- [Twinkle] Give me my son!
- [Angelo crying]

1883
01:32:56,196 --> 01:32:57,947
- Ma!
- He's my son!

1884
01:32:58,031 --> 01:32:59,842
- [Angelo] I don't want to go!
- [Twinkle] Let him go!

1885
01:32:59,866 --> 01:33:03,119
- He's my son!
- [Mama M] You're hurting him!

1886
01:33:03,203 --> 01:33:05,705
- [Angelo grunting]
- [Twinkle] Angelo!

1887
01:33:05,789 --> 01:33:08,249
Angelo! Wait!

1888
01:33:09,876 --> 01:33:12,086
- Come here. Come here.
- [Twinkle] Enough!

1889
01:33:12,170 --> 01:33:15,006
You're hurting him. Enough!

1890
01:33:15,089 --> 01:33:18,760
Enough. Okay, I'll let him go!

1891
01:33:18,843 --> 01:33:20,595
I'll let him go.

1892
01:33:21,137 --> 01:33:22,847
Enough.

1893
01:33:23,556 --> 01:33:25,391
Angelo!

1894
01:33:25,475 --> 01:33:30,355
[both crying]

1895
01:33:30,939 --> 01:33:32,565
Take him.

1896
01:33:33,149 --> 01:33:35,318
Take him. Okay, I'll cooperate.

1897
01:33:35,401 --> 01:33:36,778
Ma!

1898
01:33:36,861 --> 01:33:41,157
You said you wouldn't give me to them.

1899
01:33:41,241 --> 01:33:43,284
Are you lying to me again?

1900
01:33:43,368 --> 01:33:45,662
No, no.

1901
01:33:46,663 --> 01:33:49,415
You have to go
so you won't get hurt, Angelo.

1902
01:33:49,499 --> 01:33:51,793
I don't want to, Mama!

1903
01:33:52,335 --> 01:33:53,378
It'll just be for a while.

1904
01:33:53,461 --> 01:33:55,004
I'll come for you right away.

1905
01:33:55,088 --> 01:33:57,632
- I'll come for you! I'll fix this!
- I don't want to, Mama!

1906
01:33:57,715 --> 01:33:59,509
Angelo!

1907
01:34:00,218 --> 01:34:04,138
[Mama M] Twinkle! Twinkle! Angelo fell!

1908
01:34:05,265 --> 01:34:09,811
[somber music playing]

1909
01:34:18,444 --> 01:34:22,407
[inaudible]

1910
01:34:25,243 --> 01:34:28,079
[whimpering]

1911
01:34:28,162 --> 01:34:30,331
Ma'am, just to confirm.

1912
01:34:30,415 --> 01:34:32,750
Reyes is the last name, correct?

1913
01:34:32,834 --> 01:34:34,210
- Yes.
- Okay.

1914
01:34:34,294 --> 01:34:35,712
How's my son?

1915
01:34:35,795 --> 01:34:37,547
Ma'am, I'll update you as soon as I can,

1916
01:34:37,630 --> 01:34:40,842
but rest assured that the doctor
is doing everything he can.

1917
01:34:47,015 --> 01:34:48,474
[Mara] Twinkle!

1918
01:34:48,558 --> 01:34:50,101
Where's Angelo?

1919
01:34:53,688 --> 01:34:55,940
Mutya told me what happened.

1920
01:34:56,774 --> 01:34:57,984
Twinkle.

1921
01:34:58,067 --> 01:34:59,611
Where is he?

1922
01:35:03,656 --> 01:35:05,617
What happened to my son?

1923
01:35:06,159 --> 01:35:07,493
What happened?

1924
01:35:09,454 --> 01:35:11,831
You destroyed our lives.

1925
01:35:13,708 --> 01:35:17,795
Now Angelo is in danger
because you were selfish.

1926
01:35:19,797 --> 01:35:22,008
If you'd just handed him over
to the social workers,

1927
01:35:22,091 --> 01:35:23,009
then we wouldn't be here...

1928
01:35:23,092 --> 01:35:25,511
Who gave Angelo away to hide him?

1929
01:35:26,429 --> 01:35:28,723
You did it to protect your image

1930
01:35:28,806 --> 01:35:30,767
and your precious crown.

1931
01:35:33,937 --> 01:35:37,440
My only mistake was reconnecting with you.

1932
01:35:40,026 --> 01:35:42,779
All I needed was your signature.

1933
01:35:46,157 --> 01:35:47,867
I'm sorry, Twinkle.

1934
01:35:47,951 --> 01:35:49,869
I changed my mind.

1935
01:35:51,037 --> 01:35:52,580
I gave up the crown

1936
01:35:53,164 --> 01:35:56,125
because I realized that all these years,

1937
01:35:57,335 --> 01:35:59,921
I wanted to win not
for the title or for myself,

1938
01:36:00,004 --> 01:36:01,756
but for Angelo.

1939
01:36:02,924 --> 01:36:06,219
I thought maybe this was my opportunity

1940
01:36:06,302 --> 01:36:09,681
to make up for all my mistakes.

1941
01:36:09,764 --> 01:36:10,848
Wow.

1942
01:36:13,309 --> 01:36:15,311
What do you think he is?

1943
01:36:16,437 --> 01:36:20,650
Something that you can just
leave at the baggage counter?

1944
01:36:22,151 --> 01:36:24,654
You left him because he was too heavy?

1945
01:36:25,655 --> 01:36:27,991
Because he was embarrassing to carry?

1946
01:36:29,409 --> 01:36:31,661
You left him because
he was going to get in the way

1947
01:36:31,744 --> 01:36:33,579
of what you want to do?

1948
01:36:35,123 --> 01:36:36,165
And then what?

1949
01:36:36,249 --> 01:36:38,084
You come back after ten years

1950
01:36:38,167 --> 01:36:40,211
because you're done with everything else?

1951
01:36:40,294 --> 01:36:42,046
Because now, you are ready?

1952
01:36:45,008 --> 01:36:47,760
You abandoned a person, Mara.
Not an object.

1953
01:36:48,761 --> 01:36:50,596
Not a thing.

1954
01:36:51,848 --> 01:36:53,516
A life.

1955
01:36:56,853 --> 01:36:59,439
[Mara] I never denied that I left him.

1956
01:36:59,522 --> 01:37:00,523
Yes, you did!

1957
01:37:00,606 --> 01:37:03,484
And I know that was wrong. I accept that.

1958
01:37:03,568 --> 01:37:05,445
My life was a mess back then, Twinkle.

1959
01:37:05,528 --> 01:37:06,904
You know that.

1960
01:37:07,488 --> 01:37:09,157
I didn't know what to do.

1961
01:37:09,240 --> 01:37:11,034
Cut the crap, Mara.

1962
01:37:12,410 --> 01:37:14,829
I think about him every single day.

1963
01:37:14,912 --> 01:37:17,540
You only thought about him!

1964
01:37:19,417 --> 01:37:22,545
You think it's enough that
you thought about him?

1965
01:37:24,297 --> 01:37:27,550
Motherhood isn't just about thinking.

1966
01:37:27,633 --> 01:37:29,594
It's about doing.

1967
01:37:29,677 --> 01:37:31,929
I still gave birth to Angelo.

1968
01:37:34,015 --> 01:37:35,808
I'm his real mother.

1969
01:37:35,892 --> 01:37:38,853
You only carried him for nine months.

1970
01:37:41,355 --> 01:37:45,651
But I've been taking care of him
for ten years, every day.

1971
01:37:47,570 --> 01:37:51,032
I will never give birth
because I'm not a woman.

1972
01:37:52,116 --> 01:37:54,327
But I am a mother.

1973
01:37:54,952 --> 01:37:56,871
I am a mother, Mara!

1974
01:37:56,954 --> 01:37:58,831
I am his mother.

1975
01:37:58,915 --> 01:38:02,335
I'm his mother because he chose me.

1976
01:38:02,835 --> 01:38:07,840
He chose me
the moment he spoke his very first word.

1977
01:38:08,758 --> 01:38:09,926
"Mama."

1978
01:38:11,135 --> 01:38:12,135
"Mama."

1979
01:38:12,178 --> 01:38:14,430
He called me Mama.

1980
01:38:21,187 --> 01:38:22,855
What makes you a mother?

1981
01:38:25,274 --> 01:38:27,026
Did you endure anything?

1982
01:38:28,778 --> 01:38:31,072
Are you hurting?

1983
01:38:32,615 --> 01:38:34,951
Do you worry so much
when he's not with you?

1984
01:38:35,034 --> 01:38:38,704
You don't know how scared I get
when he is not well.

1985
01:38:39,413 --> 01:38:44,001
All the saints
I call on when he gets sick.

1986
01:38:45,128 --> 01:38:49,048
Have you ever begged for money
just to meet his needs?

1987
01:38:49,132 --> 01:38:52,802
Have you ever been humiliated because you
couldn't pay back the money you borrowed?

1988
01:38:52,885 --> 01:38:56,764
- You win! You're the one who sacrificed!
- For his field trip?

1989
01:38:57,265 --> 01:38:58,474
That's right!

1990
01:38:59,308 --> 01:39:01,352
I did sacrifice!

1991
01:39:08,484 --> 01:39:10,653
Could you sell a part of your body

1992
01:39:10,736 --> 01:39:13,072
just to extend his life?

1993
01:39:15,449 --> 01:39:17,076
I could

1994
01:39:17,160 --> 01:39:19,328
because I'm his mother.

1995
01:39:23,791 --> 01:39:26,043
But I'm his mother too!

1996
01:39:29,213 --> 01:39:32,216
I want to do all of that for him too!

1997
01:39:34,177 --> 01:39:36,262
All I'm asking for is a chance.

1998
01:39:36,345 --> 01:39:38,639
Of the two of us, you were the one
given the first chance.

1999
01:39:38,723 --> 01:39:40,391
But you didn't want it, remember?

2000
01:39:44,020 --> 01:39:46,230
The moment they cut the cord between you,

2001
01:39:46,314 --> 01:39:50,067
you ended your motherhood
because you didn't want him.

2002
01:39:52,653 --> 01:39:55,990
And from that moment,
his heart was connected to mine.

2003
01:40:01,495 --> 01:40:04,874
Angelo and I share one life, Mara.

2004
01:40:09,545 --> 01:40:11,756
Angelo is my whole world.

2005
01:40:11,839 --> 01:40:14,884
[sobbing]

2006
01:40:23,184 --> 01:40:24,852
Mara…

2007
01:40:27,605 --> 01:40:29,774
I'm begging you.

2008
01:40:31,192 --> 01:40:34,153
Please, don't take him away from me.

2009
01:40:46,832 --> 01:40:50,503
[both sobbing]

2010
01:40:53,297 --> 01:40:54,632
Please, Mara.

2011
01:40:54,715 --> 01:40:57,760
[doctor] Excuse me,
I'm really sorry to interrupt.

2012
01:40:58,386 --> 01:41:00,596
The child needs a blood transfusion.

2013
01:41:02,181 --> 01:41:04,642
We're having difficulty
because he's O-negative.

2014
01:41:04,725 --> 01:41:07,436
- If by any chance, one of you...
- I'm O-negative, Doc.

2015
01:41:08,062 --> 01:41:09,355
I'm the mother.

2016
01:41:10,690 --> 01:41:12,566
Please let me save my child.

2017
01:41:13,943 --> 01:41:15,111
[doctor] All right.

2018
01:41:15,194 --> 01:41:16,279
This way, please.

2019
01:41:21,951 --> 01:41:23,077
Excuse me.

2020
01:41:56,569 --> 01:42:02,116
[morose music playing]

2021
01:42:04,493 --> 01:42:05,494
[bead clatters]

2022
01:42:13,169 --> 01:42:18,841
[morose music continues]

2023
01:42:24,597 --> 01:42:26,974
[Twinkle] <i>I thought</i>
<i>I could give him everything.</i>

2024
01:42:29,727 --> 01:42:31,187
<i>But in the end,</i>

2025
01:42:33,147 --> 01:42:36,484
I still couldn't prove that
I'm Angelo's mother.

2026
01:42:37,401 --> 01:42:40,988
Don't doubt yourself as a mother.

2027
01:42:41,697 --> 01:42:43,407
[Mama M] <i>You have been a good mother.</i>

2028
01:42:43,491 --> 01:42:45,326
<i>I am a witness to it.</i>

2029
01:42:54,168 --> 01:42:56,545
[Twinkle] <i>But they won't see that.</i>

2030
01:42:58,923 --> 01:43:01,008
[Mama M] <i>You're Angelo's mother.</i>

2031
01:43:01,926 --> 01:43:04,428
<i>Nothing can erase that.</i>

2032
01:43:06,639 --> 01:43:09,183
<i>But we have to accept</i>

2033
01:43:10,226 --> 01:43:12,686
that Mara is also his mother.

2034
01:43:14,480 --> 01:43:17,149
Don't take that away from her.

2035
01:43:21,070 --> 01:43:27,326
- [wailing]
- [morose music continues]

2036
01:43:44,802 --> 01:43:50,516
- [monitor beeping]
- [morose music continues]

2037
01:44:00,943 --> 01:44:03,737
[Twinkle] <i>I love my son so much, Mara.</i>

2038
01:44:06,740 --> 01:44:10,536
<i>All I ever wanted was what's best for him.</i>

2039
01:44:17,793 --> 01:44:19,795
<i>I don't want him confused or hurt</i>

2040
01:44:19,879 --> 01:44:22,465
<i>just because we are fighting over him.</i>

2041
01:44:31,182 --> 01:44:32,808
<i>I'll step back.</i>

2042
01:44:36,061 --> 01:44:37,396
<i>I'll walk away.</i>

2043
01:44:40,691 --> 01:44:42,443
<i>I only ask one thing of you.</i>

2044
01:44:45,404 --> 01:44:48,115
<i>Please don't erase me from his life.</i>

2045
01:44:50,534 --> 01:44:55,456
<i>Please don't let him forget
that I am his mother too.</i>

2046
01:45:07,635 --> 01:45:10,179
Shall we eat?
What's your favorite restaurant?

2047
01:45:13,724 --> 01:45:15,559
Mama!

2048
01:45:16,185 --> 01:45:17,245
[Anton] I'll just get the car.

2049
01:45:17,269 --> 01:45:20,898
See? I knew you wouldn't lie.

2050
01:45:20,981 --> 01:45:22,691
Let's go home.

2051
01:45:27,488 --> 01:45:30,533
Sweetie, Mara and I talked.

2052
01:45:30,616 --> 01:45:32,326
You made up?

2053
01:45:34,203 --> 01:45:36,330
[Angelo] Yay!

2054
01:45:39,124 --> 01:45:41,210
Since we made up,

2055
01:45:41,293 --> 01:45:43,796
we've decided that…

2056
01:45:47,383 --> 01:45:49,635
I won't continue
with the adoption anymore.

2057
01:45:52,388 --> 01:45:53,514
Mama?

2058
01:45:54,723 --> 01:45:57,184
I want you two
to spend some time together.

2059
01:45:57,685 --> 01:45:59,603
So you can get to know each other better.

2060
01:46:00,145 --> 01:46:02,690
Isn't that great? You get two moms.

2061
01:46:03,190 --> 01:46:05,734
She's your mom, I'm your mom.
Don't you like that?

2062
01:46:08,237 --> 01:46:09,363
[Mara] Angelo?

2063
01:46:11,198 --> 01:46:13,409
You'll stay with us for now, okay?

2064
01:46:15,578 --> 01:46:16,954
[sobs] Mama,

2065
01:46:18,497 --> 01:46:20,040
I don't want to.

2066
01:46:20,874 --> 01:46:22,585
I want to be with you.

2067
01:46:23,168 --> 01:46:25,963
Let's go home to our house.

2068
01:46:27,131 --> 01:46:29,508
You're the only mom I want.

2069
01:46:32,177 --> 01:46:33,429
I'm not going away.

2070
01:46:33,512 --> 01:46:34,888
I'm always right here.

2071
01:46:36,307 --> 01:46:38,100
I'll be right here.

2072
01:46:39,226 --> 01:46:40,894
I don't want that, Mama!

2073
01:46:40,978 --> 01:46:42,896
[Angelo] I don't want that!

2074
01:46:42,980 --> 01:46:44,523
[Twinkle] There's no way.

2075
01:46:44,607 --> 01:46:47,943
Mama has work in Hong Kong.
Remember, I got hired there?

2076
01:46:48,986 --> 01:46:50,946
So I have to go.

2077
01:46:51,947 --> 01:46:54,241
I'll go with you.

2078
01:46:54,908 --> 01:46:57,745
Please don't leave me!

2079
01:46:58,370 --> 01:47:00,748
Don't you want me anymore?

2080
01:47:00,831 --> 01:47:03,292
Don't you love me anymore?

2081
01:47:03,375 --> 01:47:04,877
[Twinkle] I do!

2082
01:47:05,628 --> 01:47:08,339
I'm doing this because I love you.

2083
01:47:08,422 --> 01:47:09,923
I love you so, so much.

2084
01:47:10,007 --> 01:47:16,013
[sobbing continues]

2085
01:47:16,096 --> 01:47:16,972
Take care...

2086
01:47:17,056 --> 01:47:19,350
[Angelo crying]

2087
01:47:21,435 --> 01:47:23,020
[Angelo] I want to be with you!

2088
01:47:23,604 --> 01:47:25,481
We're leaving now.

2089
01:47:25,564 --> 01:47:27,274
I want to be with you!

2090
01:47:27,358 --> 01:47:29,276
We're leaving. Get in, okay?

2091
01:47:29,360 --> 01:47:30,378
[Twinkle] Where's the car?

2092
01:47:30,402 --> 01:47:32,446
[Angelo] I want to be with you!

2093
01:47:32,529 --> 01:47:34,365
[Mara] Angelo, let's go.

2094
01:47:34,448 --> 01:47:35,783
[Twinkle] Let's go, get in.

2095
01:47:36,450 --> 01:47:38,827
- I want to be with you!
- Come on, sweetie.

2096
01:47:39,662 --> 01:47:40,579
[Twinkle] Get in the car.

2097
01:47:40,663 --> 01:47:42,790
[Angelo] I want to be with you!

2098
01:47:42,873 --> 01:47:43,791
Time to go.

2099
01:47:43,874 --> 01:47:45,250
- Angelo.
- Get in the car.

2100
01:47:45,334 --> 01:47:46,627
Mama!

2101
01:47:46,710 --> 01:47:47,628
[Twinkle] Bye!

2102
01:47:47,711 --> 01:47:49,546
- Angelo, let's go.
- [Angelo] Mama!

2103
01:47:49,630 --> 01:47:52,800
- Please, sweetheart. Let go now.
- Come on. Don't be stubborn.

2104
01:47:52,883 --> 01:47:56,428
Mama, I want to be with you!

2105
01:47:57,304 --> 01:47:58,639
Mama!

2106
01:47:58,722 --> 01:48:01,058
Bye.

2107
01:48:01,141 --> 01:48:03,560
[Angelo] I don't want to!

2108
01:48:05,396 --> 01:48:07,272
Mama, I want to be with you!

2109
01:48:07,356 --> 01:48:09,000
- [Twinkle] It's okay, son.
- [Angelo wailing]

2110
01:48:09,024 --> 01:48:11,860
Mama! [Sobs]

2111
01:48:14,363 --> 01:48:18,784
- Mama!
- Bye.

2112
01:48:19,785 --> 01:48:22,037
[mouths] I love you.

2113
01:48:22,746 --> 01:48:26,583
[emotional music playing]

2114
01:48:29,712 --> 01:48:32,715
Mama!

2115
01:48:32,798 --> 01:48:34,675
[Angelo keeps sobbing] Ma!

2116
01:48:35,426 --> 01:48:37,428
Mama!

2117
01:48:37,511 --> 01:48:39,930
Angelo, stop crying.

2118
01:48:42,641 --> 01:48:45,060
- Mama!
- Hush now.

2119
01:48:50,023 --> 01:48:52,818
[whimpers]

2120
01:49:06,123 --> 01:49:10,794
[whimsical music playing]

2121
01:49:44,912 --> 01:49:50,793
[whimsical music continues]

2122
01:50:04,807 --> 01:50:05,807
Project.

2123
01:50:06,350 --> 01:50:07,726
Shoulders back.

2124
01:50:07,810 --> 01:50:10,312
Make them feel your joy.

2125
01:50:11,104 --> 01:50:13,398
Janine, your lipstick.

2126
01:50:14,691 --> 01:50:16,443
Jaylo, fix your collar, please.

2127
01:50:17,945 --> 01:50:21,114
Everyone, don't forget to smile.

2128
01:50:21,198 --> 01:50:22,866
- Yes, Twinkle!
- Yes, Twinkle!

2129
01:50:22,950 --> 01:50:24,076
[claps]

2130
01:50:33,210 --> 01:50:35,130
[Twinkle]<i> What does it truly mean</i>
<i>to be a mother?</i>

2131
01:50:36,255 --> 01:50:39,007
<i>Is it when you give birth?</i>

2132
01:50:39,633 --> 01:50:43,178
<i>Or is it when you raise the child?</i>

2133
01:50:45,556 --> 01:50:48,392
<i>It was here, in Hong Kong,
that I finally understood,</i>

2134
01:50:48,475 --> 01:50:54,356
<i>being a mother isn't about
gender, distance,</i>

2135
01:50:54,439 --> 01:50:55,566
<i>or blood.</i>

2136
01:50:56,817 --> 01:50:59,945
<i>Being a mother is about the heart.</i>

2137
01:51:02,990 --> 01:51:05,951
<i>They may be away from each other.</i>

2138
01:51:07,119 --> 01:51:09,079
<i>- But the love endures.</i>
- [mouths] Mama!

2139
01:51:14,668 --> 01:51:16,461
[mouths] Angelo!

2140
01:51:16,545 --> 01:51:18,589
[Twinkle] <i>Because a mother's love</i>

2141
01:51:19,381 --> 01:51:21,049
<i>is for life.</i>

2142
01:51:22,718 --> 01:51:25,262
[both chuckle]

2143
01:51:25,345 --> 01:51:26,388
I'm surprised!

2144
01:51:26,471 --> 01:51:28,682
- When did you get here?
- Just now.

2145
01:51:28,765 --> 01:51:30,517
He wanted to see you right away.

2146
01:51:30,601 --> 01:51:32,185
School's done, Ma.

2147
01:51:32,269 --> 01:51:34,897
I can spend my vacation with you now!

2148
01:51:34,980 --> 01:51:36,861
- [Mara chuckles]
- Stay here with me, sweetheart.

2149
01:51:36,940 --> 01:51:38,710
I won't return you
to your mommy anymore, okay?

2150
01:51:38,734 --> 01:51:40,527
- [Mara] I heard that!
- Just stay here.

2151
01:51:41,403 --> 01:51:43,071
What's that?

2152
01:51:43,155 --> 01:51:44,573
Your electricity bill?

2153
01:51:44,656 --> 01:51:45,782
[chuckles]

2154
01:51:45,866 --> 01:51:46,909
Be our godmother.

2155
01:51:46,992 --> 01:51:49,220
I don't want to be a godmother.
I want to be a flower girl!

2156
01:51:49,244 --> 01:51:50,287
[Twinkle and Mara chuckle]

2157
01:51:50,370 --> 01:51:51,622
I love you, Mama.

2158
01:51:51,705 --> 01:51:53,248
I missed you so much!

2159
01:51:53,332 --> 01:51:55,542
["Tala" by Bryan Chong playing]

2160
01:51:55,626 --> 01:51:56,877
Music to my ears!

2161
01:51:56,960 --> 01:51:58,921
Tell me again, please!

2162
01:51:59,004 --> 01:52:00,505
I love you, Mama!

2163
01:52:00,589 --> 01:52:01,715
I love you too!

2164
01:52:01,798 --> 01:52:04,301
I love you! I love you!
I missed you!

2165
01:52:04,384 --> 01:52:08,764
["Tala" continues]

2166
01:52:08,847 --> 01:52:10,891
I love you!

2167
01:52:11,767 --> 01:52:12,893
Kiss! Kiss!

2168
01:52:12,976 --> 01:52:14,686
[laughs]

2169
01:52:16,313 --> 01:52:19,733
- ["Tala" continues]
- [fireworks exploding]

2170
01:52:19,816 --> 01:52:22,694
[Twinkle] Look, baby, so many colors!

2171
01:52:23,487 --> 01:52:26,114
[laughs fondly]

2172
01:52:31,536 --> 01:52:33,205
Give me a kiss!

2173
01:52:33,288 --> 01:52:35,123
[happy laugh]

2174
01:52:40,671 --> 01:52:43,340
["Tala" continues]

2175
01:52:45,842 --> 01:52:48,428
[fireworks continue]

2176
01:53:08,740 --> 01:53:10,617
[Twinkle] <i>So, Angelo, my son,</i>

2177
01:53:11,243 --> 01:53:13,203
<i>no matter how far apart we are,</i>

2178
01:53:13,996 --> 01:53:16,081
<i>I'm still your mom, okay?</i>

2179
01:53:16,999 --> 01:53:19,084
<i>Because you're always right here,</i>

2180
01:53:20,043 --> 01:53:21,878
<i>inside my heart.</i>

2181
01:53:21,962 --> 01:53:27,884
["Tala" continues]

2182
01:53:48,113 --> 01:53:49,114
[camera clicks]

2183
01:53:49,197 --> 01:53:54,953
[song fades]

2184
01:53:58,665 --> 01:54:04,421
["Tala" by Bryan Chong playing]

2185
02:00:35,645 --> 02:00:37,021
[song fades]

